\li1 \v 62 \rb These men|אֵ֗לֶּה\rb* \rb searched for|בִּקְשׁ֧וּ\rb* \rb their family records|כְתָבָ֛ם\rb*\rb |הַמִּתְיַחְשִׂ֖ים\rb*, \rb but they could not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb find them|נִמְצָ֑אוּ\rb* \rb and so were excluded|וַֽיְגֹאֲל֖וּ\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the priesthood as unclean|הַכְּהֻנָּֽה׃\rb*. \v 63 \rb The governor|הַתִּרְשָׁ֙תָא֙\rb* \rb ordered|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb not|לֹא־\rb* \rb to eat|יֹאכְל֖וּ\rb* \rb the most holy things|מִקֹּ֣דֶשׁ\rb*\rb |הַקֳּדָשִׁ֑ים\rb* \rb until|עַ֛ד\rb*\rb |עֲמֹ֥ד\rb* \rb there was a priest|כֹּהֵ֖ן\rb* \rb to consult the Urim|לְאוּרִ֥ים\rb* \rb and Thummim|וּלְתֻמִּֽים׃\rb*.\f + \fr 2:63 \ft Literally \fqa Lights and Perfections\f*
\p \v 64 \rb The whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb assembly|הַקָּהָ֖ל\rb* \rb numbered|כְּאֶחָ֑ד\rb* \rb 42,360|אַרְבַּ֣ע\rb*\rb |רִבּ֔וֹא\rb*\rb |אַלְפַּ֖יִם\rb*\rb |שְׁלֹשׁ־\rb*\rb |מֵא֥וֹת\rb*\rb |שִׁשִּֽׁים׃\rb*, \v 65 \rb in addition to|מִ֠לְּבַד\rb*\rb |אֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb their 7,337|שִׁבְעַ֣ת\rb*\rb |אֲלָפִ֔ים\rb*\rb |שְׁלֹ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |מֵא֖וֹת\rb*\rb |שְׁלֹשִׁ֣ים\rb*\rb |וְשִׁבְעָ֑ה\rb* \rb menservants|עַבְדֵיהֶ֤ם\rb* \rb and maidservants|וְאַמְהֹֽתֵיהֶם֙\rb*, \rb as well as their 200|מָאתָֽיִם׃\rb* \rb male|מְשֹׁרְרִ֥ים\rb* \rb and female singers|וּֽמְשֹׁרְר֖וֹת\rb*. \v 66 \rb They had 736|שְׁבַ֥ע\rb*\rb |מֵא֖וֹת\rb*\rb |שְׁלֹשִׁ֣ים\rb*\rb |וְשִׁשָּׁ֑ה\rb* \rb horses|סוּסֵיהֶ֕ם\rb*, \rb 245|מָאתַ֖יִם\rb*\rb |אַרְבָּעִ֥ים\rb*\rb |וַחֲמִשָּֽׁה׃\rb* \rb mules|פִּרְדֵיהֶ֕ם\rb*, \v 67 \rb 435|אַרְבַּ֥ע\rb*\rb |מֵא֖וֹת\rb*\rb |שְׁלֹשִׁ֣ים\rb*\rb |וַחֲמִשָּׁ֑ה\rb* \rb camels|גְּמַ֨לֵּיהֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb and 6,720|שֵׁ֣שֶׁת\rb*\rb |אֲלָפִ֔ים\rb*\rb |שְׁבַ֥ע\rb*\rb |מֵא֖וֹת\rb*\rb |וְעֶשְׂרִֽים׃פ\rb* \rb donkeys|חֲמֹרִ֕ים\rb*.
\s1 Offerings by the Exiles
\p \v 68 \rb When they arrived|בְּבוֹאָ֕ם\rb* \rb at the house|לְבֵ֥ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb*, \rb some of the heads|וּמֵרָאשֵׁי֙\rb* \rb of the families|הָֽאָב֔וֹת\rb* \rb gave freewill offerings|הִֽתְנַדְּבוּ֙\rb* \rb to rebuild|לְהַעֲמִיד֖וֹ\rb* \rb the house|לְבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of God|הָֽאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb its original site|מְכוֹנֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 69 \rb According to their ability|כְּכֹחָ֗ם\rb*, \rb they gave|נָתְנוּ֮\rb* \rb to the treasury|לְאוֹצַ֣ר\rb* \rb for this work|הַמְּלָאכָה֒\rb* \rb 61,000|שֵׁשׁ־\rb*\rb |רִבֹּ֣אות\rb*\rb |וָאֶ֔לֶףס\rb* \rb darics|דַּרְכְּמוֹנִים֙\rb* \rb of gold|זָהָ֗ב\rb*,\f + \fr 2:69 \ft Or \fqa 61,000 gold drachmas\ft ; that is, approximately 1,129.7 pounds or 512.4 kilograms of gold coins\f* \rb 5,000|חֲמֵ֣שֶׁת\rb*\rb |אֲלָפִ֑ים\rb* \rb minas|מָנִ֖ים\rb* \rb of silver|וְכֶ֕סֶף\rb*,\f + \fr 2:69 \fqa 5,000 minas \ft is approximately 3.14 tons or 2.85 metric tons of silver.\f* \rb and 100|מֵאָֽה׃ס\rb* \rb priestly|כֹּהֲנִ֖ים\rb* \rb garments|וְכָתְנֹ֥ת\rb*.
\p \v 70 \rb So the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֣ים\rb*, \rb the Levites|וְ֠הַלְוִיִּם\rb*, \rb the singers|וְהַמְשֹׁרְרִ֧ים\rb*, \rb the gatekeepers|וְהַשּׁוֹעֲרִ֛ים\rb*, \rb and the temple servants|וְהַנְּתִינִ֖ים\rb*, \rb along with some|וּֽמִן־\rb* \rb of the people|הָעָ֞ם\rb*, \rb settled|וַיֵּשְׁב֣וּ\rb* \rb in their own towns|בְּעָרֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*; \rb and the rest|וְכָל־\rb* \rb of the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*\f + \fr 2:70 \ft Or \fqa all Israel\f* \rb settled in their towns|בְּעָרֵיהֶֽם׃ס\rb*.
\c 3
\s1 Sacrifices Restored
\p \v 1 \rb By the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִ֔י\rb* \rb month|הַחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb the Israelites|וּבְנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb had settled|וַיִּגַּע֙\rb* \rb in their towns|בֶּעָרִ֑יםס\rb*, \rb and the people|הָעָ֛ם\rb* \rb assembled|וַיֵּאָסְפ֥וּ\rb* \rb as one|אֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb man|כְּאִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָֽם׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 2 \rb Then Jeshua|יֵשׁ֨וּעַ\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jozadak|יֽוֹצָדָ֜ק\rb*\f + \fr 3:2 \fqa Jozadak \ft is a variant of \fqa Jehozadak\ft ; also in verse 8; see 1 Chronicles 6:14.\f* \rb and his fellow|וְאֶחָ֣יו\rb* \rb priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֗ים\rb*, \rb along with Zerubbabel|וּזְרֻבָּבֶ֤ל\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Shealtiel|שְׁאַלְתִּיאֵל֙\rb* \rb and his associates|וְאֶחָ֔יו\rb*, \rb began|וַיָּקָם֩\rb* \rb to build|וַיִּבְנ֕וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the altar|מִזְבַּ֖ח\rb* \rb of the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb to sacrifice|לְהַעֲל֤וֹת\rb* \rb burnt offerings|עֹל֔וֹת\rb* \rb on it|עָלָיו֙\rb*, \rb as it is written|כַּכָּת֕וּב\rb* \rb in the Law|בְּתוֹרַ֖ת\rb* \rb of Moses|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb* \rb the man|אִישׁ־\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb*. \v 3 \rb They set up|וַיָּכִ֤ינוּ\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֙חַ֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb its foundation|מְכ֣וֹנֹתָ֔יו\rb* \rb and sacrificed|וַיַּעַל\rb*\rb |עָלָ֤יו\rb* \rb burnt offerings|עֹלוֹת֙\rb* \rb on it|עֲלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֔ה\rb* — \rb both the morning|לַבֹּ֥קֶר\rb* \rb and evening|וְלָעָֽרֶב׃\rb* \rb burnt offerings|עֹל֖וֹת\rb* — \rb even though|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb they feared|בְּאֵימָ֣ה\rb* \rb the people|מֵעַמֵּ֖י\rb* \rb of the land|הָאֲרָצ֑וֹת\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb They also celebrated|וַֽיַּעֲשׂ֛וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Feast|חַ֥ג\rb* \rb of Tabernacles|הַסֻּכּ֖וֹת\rb*\f + \fr 3:4 \ft That is, Sukkot, the autumn feast of pilgrimage to Jerusalem; also translated as \fqa the Feast of Booths \ft or \fqa the Feast of Shelters \ft and originally called \fqa the Feast of Ingathering\ft (see Exodus 23:16 and Exodus 34:22).\f* \rb in accordance with what is written|כַּכָּת֑וּב\rb*, \rb and they offered burnt offerings|וְעֹלַ֨ת\rb* \rb daily|י֤וֹם\rb*\rb |בְּיוֹם֙\rb* \rb based on the number|בְּמִסְפָּ֔ר\rb* \rb prescribed|כְּמִשְׁפַּ֖ט\rb*\rb |דְּבַר־\rb* \rb for each day|י֥וֹם\rb*\rb |בְּיוֹמֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb After that|וְאַחֲרֵיכֵ֞ן\rb*, \rb they presented the regular|תָּמִיד֙\rb* \rb burnt offerings|עֹלַ֤ת\rb* \rb and those for New Moons|וְלֶ֣חֳדָשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb and for all|וּלְכָל־\rb* \rb the appointed|מוֹעֲדֵ֥י\rb* \rb sacred feasts|הַמְקֻדָּשִׁ֑ים\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb as well as all|וּלְכֹ֛ל\rb* \rb the freewill offerings|נְדָבָ֖ה\rb* \rb brought|מִתְנַדֵּ֥ב\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb On the first|אֶחָד֙\rb* \rb day|מִיּ֤וֹם\rb* \rb of the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִ֔י\rb* \rb month|לַחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb the Israelites began|הֵחֵ֕לּוּ\rb* \rb to offer|לְהַעֲל֥וֹת\rb* \rb burnt offerings|עֹל֖וֹת\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb although the foundation of the temple|וְהֵיכַ֥ל\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |לֹ֥א\rb* \rb had not been laid|יֻסָּֽד׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb They gave|וַיִּ֨תְּנוּ־\rb* \rb money|כֶ֔סֶף\rb* \rb to the masons|לַחֹצְבִ֖ים\rb* \rb and carpenters|וְלֶחָרָשִׁ֑ים\rb*, \rb and food|וּמַאֲכָ֨ל\rb* \rb and drink|וּמִשְׁתֶּ֜ה\rb* \rb and oil|וָשֶׁ֗מֶן\rb* \rb to the people of Sidon|לַצִּֽדֹנִים֙\rb* \rb and Tyre|וְלַצֹּרִ֔ים\rb* \rb to bring|לְהָבִיא֩\rb* \rb cedar|אֲרָזִ֤ים\rb* \rb logs|עֲצֵ֨י\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb Lebanon|הַלְּבָנוֹן֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joppa|יָפ֔וֹא\rb* \rb by sea|יָ֣ם\rb*, \rb as authorized|כְּרִשְׁי֛וֹן\rb*\rb |עֲלֵיהֶֽם׃פ\rb* \rb by Cyrus|כּ֥וֹרֶשׁ\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Persia|פָּרַ֖ס\rb*.
\s1 Temple Restoration Begins
\p \v 8 \rb In the second|הַשֵּׁנִ֑י\rb* \rb month|בַּחֹ֖דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of the second|הַשֵּׁנִ֗ית\rb* \rb year|וּבַשָּׁנָ֣ה\rb* \rb after they had arrived|לְבוֹאָ֞ם\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֤ית\rb* \rb of God|הָֽאֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|לִיר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb*, \rb Zerubbabel|זְרֻבָּבֶ֣ל\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Shealtiel|שְׁ֠אַלְתִּיאֵל\rb*, \rb Jeshua|וְיֵשׁ֨וּעַ\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jozadak|יֽוֹצָדָ֜ק\rb*, \rb and the rest|וּשְׁאָ֥ר\rb* \rb of their associates|אֲחֵיהֶ֣ם׀\rb* \rb including the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֣ים\rb*, \rb the Levites|וְהַלְוִיִּ֗ם\rb*, \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb who had returned|הַבָּאִים֙\rb* \rb to Jerusalem|יְרֽוּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb from the captivity|מֵהַשְּׁבִ֣י\rb*, \rb began the work|הֵחֵ֡לּוּ\rb*. \rb They appointed|וַיַּעֲמִ֣ידוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֗ם\rb* \rb twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֤ים\rb* \rb years of age|מִבֶּ֨ן\rb*\rb |שָׁנָה֙\rb* \rb or older|וָמַ֔עְלָה\rb* \rb to supervise|לְנַצֵּ֖חַ\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb the construction|מְלֶ֥אכֶת\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃פ\rb*. \v 9 \rb So Jeshua|יֵשׁ֡וּעַ\rb* \rb and his sons|בָּנָ֣יו\rb* \rb and brothers|וְ֠אֶחָיו\rb*, \rb Kadmiel|קַדְמִיאֵ֨ל\rb* \rb and his sons|וּבָנָ֤יו\rb* (\rb descendants|בְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Yehudah|יְהוּדָה֙\rb*),\f + \fr 3:9 \ft Hebrew \fqa sons of Judah\ft ; that is, most likely, \fqa sons of Yehudah\ft , another name for \fqa Hodevah \ft or \fqa Hodaviah\ft ; see Ezra 2:40 and Nehemiah 7:43.\f* \rb and the sons|בְּנֵי֙\rb* \rb of Henadad|חֵֽנָדָ֔ד\rb* \rb and their sons|בְּנֵיהֶ֥ם\rb* \rb and brothers|וַאֲחֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* — \rb all Levites|הַלְוִיִּֽם׃\rb* — \rb joined|וַיַּעֲמֹ֣ד\rb* \rb together|כְּאֶחָ֔ד\rb* \rb to supervise|לְנַצֵּ֛חַ\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb those working|עֹשֵׂ֥ה\rb*\rb |הַמְּלָאכָ֖ה\rb* \rb on the house|בְּבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֑יםס\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb When the builders|הַבֹּנִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had laid the foundation|וְיִסְּד֥וּ\rb* \rb of the temple|הֵיכַ֣ל\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֨ים\rb* \rb in their apparel|מְלֻבָּשִׁ֜ים\rb* \rb with trumpets|בַּחֲצֹֽצְר֗וֹת\rb*, \rb and the Levites|וְהַלְוִיִּ֤ם\rb* (\rb the sons|בְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Asaph|אָסָף֙\rb*) \rb with cymbals|בַּֽמְצִלְתַּ֔יִם\rb*, \rb took their positions|וַיַּעֲמִידוּ֩\rb* \rb to praise|לְהַלֵּל֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb as|עַל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֥יד\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \rb had prescribed|יְדֵ֖י\rb*. \v 11 \rb And they sang responsively|וַֽ֠יַּעֲנוּ\rb* \rb with praise|בְּהַלֵּ֨ל\rb* \rb and thanksgiving|וּבְהוֹדֹ֤ת\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָה֙\rb*:
\b 
\q1 “\rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb He is good|ט֔וֹב\rb*;
\q2 \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb His loving devotion|חַסְדּ֖וֹ\rb*\f + \fr 3:11 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa chesed \ft are translated here and in most cases throughout the Scriptures as \fqa loving devotion\ft ; the range of meaning includes \fqa love\ft , \fqa goodness\ft , \fqa kindness\ft , \fqa faithfulness\ft , and \fqa mercy\ft , as well as \fqa loyalty to a covenant\ft .\f* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb endures forever|לְעוֹלָ֥ם\rb*.”
\p \rb Then all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֡ם\rb* \rb gave a great|גְדוֹלָ֤ה\rb* \rb shout|הֵרִיעוּ֩\rb*\rb |תְרוּעָ֙ה\rb* \rb of praise|בְהַלֵּל֙\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb because the foundation|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb* \rb had been laid|הוּסַ֥ד\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb But many|וְרַבִּ֡ים\rb* \rb of the older|הַזְּקֵנִ֗ים\rb* \rb priests|מֵהַכֹּהֲנִ֣ים\rb*, \rb Levites|וְהַלְוִיִּם֩\rb*, \rb and family|הָאָב֜וֹת\rb* \rb heads|וְרָאשֵׁ֨י\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb had seen|רָא֜וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the first|הָֽרִאשׁוֹן֙\rb* \rb temple|הַבַּ֤יִת\rb* \rb wept|בֹּכִ֖ים\rb* \rb loudly|בְּק֣וֹל\rb*\rb |גָּד֑וֹל\rb* \rb when they saw|בְּעֵ֣ינֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb the foundation|בְּיָסְד֔וֹ\rb* \rb of this|זֶ֤ה\rb* \rb temple|הַבַּ֙יִת֙\rb*. \rb Still, many|וְרַבִּ֛ים\rb* \rb others shouted|בִּתְרוּעָ֥ה\rb*\rb |לְהָרִ֥ים\rb* \rb joyfully|קֽוֹל׃\rb*\rb |בְשִׂמְחָ֖ה\rb*. \v 13 \rb The people|הָעָ֗ם\rb* \rb could not|וְאֵ֣ין\rb* \rb distinguish|מַכִּירִים֙\rb*\rb |ק֚וֹל\rb* \rb the shouts|תְּרוּעַ֣ת\rb* \rb of joy|הַשִּׂמְחָ֔ה\rb* \rb from the sound|לְק֖וֹל\rb* \rb of weeping|בְּכִ֣י\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb*\rb |הָעָ֗ם\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֑ם\rb* \rb were making so much noise|מְרִיעִים֙\rb*\rb |תְּרוּעָ֣ה\rb*\rb |גְדוֹלָ֔ה\rb*. \rb And the sound|וְהַקּ֥וֹל\rb* \rb was heard|נִשְׁמַ֖ע\rb* \rb from|עַד־\rb* \rb afar|לְמֵרָחֽוֹק׃פ\rb*.
\c 4
\s1 Adversaries Hinder the Work
\p \v 1 \rb When the enemies|צָרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb and Benjamin|וּבִנְיָמִ֑ן\rb* \rb heard|וַֽיִּשְׁמְע֔וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the exiles|בְנֵ֤י\rb*\rb |הַגּוֹלָה֙\rb* \rb were building|בּוֹנִ֣ים\rb* \rb a temple|הֵיכָ֔ל\rb* \rb for the LORD|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*, \v 2 \rb they approached|וַיִּגְּשׁ֨וּ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb Zerubbabel|זְרֻבָּבֶ֜ל\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb and the heads|רָאשֵׁ֣י\rb* \rb of the families|הָֽאָב֗וֹת\rb*, \rb saying|וַיֹּאמְר֤וּ\rb*\rb |לָהֶם֙\rb*, “\rb Let us build|נִבְנֶ֣ה\rb* \rb with you|עִמָּכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb*, \rb like you|כָכֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb we seek|נִדְר֖וֹשׁ\rb* \rb your God|לֵֽאלֹהֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*\rb |אֲנַ֣חְנוּ\rb* \rb and have been sacrificing|זֹבְחִ֗ים\rb* \rb to Him since|וְלֹא\rb* \rb the time|מִימֵי֙\rb* \rb of King|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Esar-haddon|חַדֹּן֙\rb* \rb of Assyria|אַשּׁ֔וּר\rb*, \rb who brought|הַמַּעֲלֶ֥ה\rb* \rb us|אֹתָ֖נוּ\rb* \rb here|פֹּֽה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 3 \rb But Zerubbabel|זְרֻבָּבֶ֜ל\rb*, \rb Jeshua|וְיֵשׁ֗וּעַ\rb*, \rb and the other|וּשְׁאָ֨ר\rb* \rb heads|רָאשֵׁ֤י\rb* \rb of the families|הָֽאָבוֹת֙\rb* \rb of Israel|לְיִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּאמֶר֩\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֨ם\rb*, “\rb You have no|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb part|לָ֣כֶם\rb* \rb with us|וָלָ֔נוּ\rb* \rb in building|לִבְנ֥וֹת\rb* \rb a house|בַּ֖יִת\rb* \rb for our God|לֵאלֹהֵ֑ינוּ\rb*, \rb since|כִּי֩\rb* \rb we|אֲנַ֨חְנוּ\rb* \rb alone|יַ֜חַד\rb* \rb must build|נִבְנֶ֗ה\rb* \rb it for the LORD|לַֽיהוָה֙\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb Cyrus|כּ֥וֹרֶשׁ\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Persia|פָּרָֽס׃\rb* \rb has commanded us|צִוָּ֔נוּ\rb*.”
\p \v 4 \rb Then|וַיְהִי֙\rb* \rb the people|עַם־\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb set out to discourage|מְרַפִּ֖ים\rb*\rb |יְדֵ֣י\rb* \rb the people|עַם־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb* \rb and make them afraid|וּמְבַלַהִים\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb to build|לִבְנֽוֹת׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb They hired|וְסֹכְרִ֧ים\rb* \rb counselors|יוֹעֲצִ֖ים\rb* \rb against them|עֲלֵיהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb to frustrate|לְהָפֵ֣ר\rb* \rb their plans|עֲצָתָ֑ם\rb* \rb throughout|כָּל־\rb* \rb the reign|יְמֵ֗י\rb* \rb of Cyrus|כּ֚וֹרֶשׁ\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Persia|פָּרַ֔ס\rb* \rb and down to|וְעַד־\rb* \rb the reign|מַלְכ֖וּת\rb* \rb of Darius|דָּרְיָ֥וֶשׁ\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Persia|פָּרָֽס׃\rb*.
\s1 Opposition under Xerxes and Artaxerxes
\p \v 6 \rb At the beginning|בִּתְחִלַּ֖ת\rb*\rb |מַלְכוּת֑וֹ\rb* \rb of the reign|וּבְמַלְכוּת֙\rb* \rb of Xerxes|אֲחַשְׁוֵר֔וֹשׁ\rb*,\f + \fr 4:6 \ft Hebrew \fqa Ahasuerus\f* \rb an accusation|שִׂטְנָ֔ה\rb* \rb was lodged|כָּתְב֣וּ\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb the people|יֹשְׁבֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb and Jerusalem|וִירוּשָׁלִָֽם׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb And in the days|וּבִימֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Artaxerxes king|אַרְתַּחְשַׁ֗שְׂתָּא\rb* \rb of Persia|פָּרָ֑ס\rb*, \rb Bishlam|בִּשְׁלָ֜ם\rb*, \rb Mithredath|מִתְרְדָ֤ת\rb*, \rb Tabeel|טָֽבְאֵל֙\rb*, \rb and the rest of|וּשְׁאָ֣ר\rb* \rb his associates|כְּנָוֹתוֹ\rb* \rb wrote a letter|כָּתַ֨ב\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb*\rb |מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Artaxerxes|אַרְתַּחְשַׁשְׂתָּא\rb*.\rb |וּכְתָב֙\rb* \rb It|הַֽנִּשְׁתְּוָ֔ן\rb* \rb was written|כָּת֥וּב\rb* \rb in Aramaic|אֲרָמִ֖ית\rb* \rb and then translated|וּמְתֻרְגָּ֥ם\rb*\rb |אֲרָמִֽית׃פ\rb*.\f + \fr 4:7 \ft The original text of Ezra 4:8 through Ezra 6:18 is in Aramaic.\f*
\p \v 8 \rb Rehum|רְח֣וּם\rb* \rb the commander|בְּעֵל־\rb*\rb |טְעֵ֗ם\rb* \rb and Shimshai|וְשִׁמְשַׁי֙\rb* \rb the scribe|סָֽפְרָ֔א\rb* \rb wrote|כְּתַ֛בוּ\rb* \rb the|חֲדָ֖ה\rb* \rb letter|אִגְּרָ֥ה\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְרוּשְׁלֶ֑ם\rb* \rb to King|מַלְכָּ֖א\rb* \rb Artaxerxes|לְאַרְתַּחְשַׁ֥שְׂתְּא\rb* \rb as follows|כְּנֵֽמָא׃\rb*:
\p \v 9 \rb |אֱדַ֜יִן\rb* \rb From Rehum|רְח֣וּם\rb* \rb the commander|בְּעֵל־\rb*\rb |טְעֵ֗ם\rb*, \rb Shimshai|וְשִׁמְשַׁי֙\rb* \rb the scribe|סָֽפְרָ֔א\rb*, \rb and the rest|וּשְׁאָ֖ר\rb* \rb of their associates|כְּנָוָתְה֑וֹן\rb*— \rb the judges|דִּ֠ינָיֵא\rb* \rb and officials|וַאֲפַרְסַתְכָיֵ֞א\rb* \rb over Tripolis|טַרְפְּלָיֵ֣א\rb*, \rb Persia|אֲפָֽרְסָיֵ֗א\rb*, \rb Erech|אַרְכְּוָי\rb* \rb and Babylon|בָבְלָיֵא֙\rb*, \rb the Elamites|עֵלְמָיֵֽא׃\rb* \rb of Susa|שֽׁוּשַׁנְכָיֵ֔א\rb*, \v 10 \rb and the rest|וּשְׁאָ֣ר\rb* \rb of the peoples|אֻמַּיָּ֗א\rb* \rb whom|דִּ֤י\rb* \rb the great|רַבָּ֣א\rb* \rb and honorable|וְיַקִּירָ֔א\rb* \rb Ashurbanipal|אָסְנַפַּר֙\rb*\f + \fr 4:10 \ft Aramaic \fqa Osnappar\ft , another name for \fqa Ashurbanipal\f* \rb deported|הַגְלִי֙\rb* \rb and settled|וְהוֹתֵ֣ב\rb*\rb |הִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb in the cities|בְּקִרְיָ֖ה\rb* \rb of|דִּ֣י\rb* \rb Samaria|שָׁמְרָ֑יִן\rb* \rb and elsewhere|וּשְׁאָ֥ר\rb* \rb west|עֲבַֽר־\rb* \rb of the Euphrates|נַהֲרָ֖ה\rb*\rb |וּכְעֶֽנֶת׃\rb*.\f + \fr 4:10 \ft Aramaic \fqa beyond the River\ft ; also in verses 11, 16, 17, and 20\f*
\p \v 11 (\rb This|דְּנָה֙\rb* \rb is the text|פַּרְשֶׁ֣גֶן\rb* \rb of the letter|אִגַּרְתָּ֔א\rb*\rb |דִּ֚י\rb* \rb they sent|שְׁלַ֣חוּ\rb* \rb to him|עֲל֔וֹהִי\rb*.)
\p \rb To|עַל־\rb* \rb King|מַלְכָּ֑א\rb* \rb Artaxerxes|אַרְתַּחְשַׁ֖שְׂתְּא\rb*,
\p \rb From your servants|עַבְדָ֛יךְ\rb*, \rb the men|אֱנָ֥שׁ\rb* \rb west|עֲבַֽר־\rb* \rb of the Euphrates|נַהֲרָ֖ה\rb*\rb |וּכְעֶֽנֶת׃פ\rb*:
\p \v 12 \rb Let it be|לֶהֱוֵ֣א\rb* \rb known|יְדִ֙יעַ֙\rb* \rb to the king|לְמַלְכָּ֔א\rb* \rb that|דִּ֣י\rb* \rb the Jews|יְהוּדָיֵ֗א\rb* \rb who|דִּ֤י\rb* \rb came|סְלִ֙קוּ֙\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb you|לְוָתָ֔ךְ\rb* \rb to us|עֲלֶ֥ינָא\rb* \rb have returned|אֲת֖וֹ\rb* \rb to Jerusalem|לִירוּשְׁלֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and are rebuilding|בָּנַ֔יִן\rb* \rb that rebellious|מָֽרָדְתָּ֤א\rb* \rb and wicked|וּבִֽאישְׁתָּא֙\rb* \rb city|קִרְיְתָ֨א\rb*. \rb They are restoring|אֲשַׁכְלְלוּ\rb* \rb its walls|וְשׁוּרַיָּ\rb* \rb and repairing|יַחִֽיטוּ׃\rb* \rb its foundations|וְאֻשַּׁיָּ֖א\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb Let it now|כְּעַ֗ן\rb* \rb be|לֶהֱוֵ֣א\rb* \rb known|יְדִ֙יעַ֙\rb* \rb to the king|לְמַלְכָּ֔א\rb* \rb that|דִּ֠י\rb* \rb if|הֵ֣ן\rb* \rb that|דָךְ֙\rb* \rb city|קִרְיְתָ֥א\rb* \rb is rebuilt|תִּתְבְּנֵ֔א\rb* \rb and its walls|וְשׁוּרַיָּ֖ה\rb* \rb are restored|יִֽשְׁתַּכְלְל֑וּן\rb*, \rb they will not|לָ֣א\rb* \rb pay|יִנְתְּנ֔וּן\rb* \rb tribute|מִנְדָּֽה־\rb*, \rb duty|בְל֤וֹ\rb*, \rb or toll|וַהֲלָךְ֙\rb*, \rb and the royal|מַלְכִ֖ים\rb* \rb treasury|וְאַפְּתֹ֥ם\rb* \rb will suffer|תְּהַנְזִֽק׃\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb Now|כְּעַ֗ן\rb* \rb because|כָּל־\rb* \rb we are in the service|מְלַ֔חְנָא\rb* \rb of the palace|הֵֽיכְלָא֙\rb*\f + \fr 4:14 \ft Literally \fqa because the salt of the palace is our salt\f*\rb |לָ֥א\rb* \rb and it is not fitting|אֲ‍ֽרִֽיךְ\rb* \rb for us|לַ֖נָא\rb* \rb to allow|לְמֶֽחֱזֵ֑א\rb*\rb |עַ֨ל־\rb*\rb |דְּנָ֔ה\rb* \rb the king|מַלְכָּ֔א\rb* \rb to be dishonored|וְעַרְוַ֣ת\rb*, \rb we have sent|שְׁלַ֖חְנָא\rb* \rb to inform|וְהוֹדַ֥עְנָא\rb* \rb the king|לְמַלְכָּֽא׃\rb* \v 15 \rb that|דִּ֡י\rb* \rb a search should be made|יְבַקַּר֩\rb* \rb of the record|דָּכְרָ֨נַיָּ֜א\rb* \rb books|בִּֽסְפַר־\rb* \rb of|דִּ֣י\rb* \rb your fathers|אֲבָהָתָ֗ךְ\rb*. \rb In these|דָּכְרָנַיָּא֮\rb* \rb books|בִּסְפַ֣ר\rb* \rb you will discover|וּ֠תְהַשְׁכַּח\rb* \rb and verify|וְתִנְדַּע֒\rb* \rb that|דִּי֩\rb* \rb the city|קִרְיְתָ֨א\rb* \rb is a rebellious|מָֽרָדָ֗א\rb* \rb city|קִרְיָ֣א\rb*, \rb harmful|וּֽמְהַנְזְקַ֤ת\rb* \rb to kings|מַלְכִין֙\rb* \rb and provinces|וּמְדִנָ֔ן\rb*, \rb inciting|עָבְדִ֣ין\rb* \rb sedition|וְאֶשְׁתַּדּוּר֙\rb*\rb |בְּגַוַּ֔הּ\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb ancient|עָלְמָ֑א\rb* \rb times|יוֹמָ֖ת\rb*. \rb That is why|עַ֨ל־\rb* \rb this|דְּנָ֔ה\rb* \rb city|קִרְיְתָ֥א\rb*\rb |דָ֖ךְ\rb* \rb was destroyed|הָֽחָרְבַֽת׃\rb*.
\p \v 16 \rb We|אֲנַ֙חְנָה֙\rb* \rb advise|מְהוֹדְעִ֤ין\rb* \rb the king|לְמַלְכָּ֔א\rb* \rb that|דִּ֠י\rb* \rb if|הֵ֣ן\rb* \rb this|דָךְ֙\rb* \rb city|קִרְיְתָ֥א\rb* \rb is rebuilt|תִּתְבְּנֵ֔א\rb* \rb and its walls|וְשׁוּרַיָּ֖ה\rb* \rb are restored|יִֽשְׁתַּכְלְל֑וּן\rb*,\rb |לָקֳבֵ֣ל\rb*\rb |דְּנָ֔ה\rb* \rb you will have|אִיתַ֖י\rb* \rb no|לָ֥א\rb*\rb |לָֽךְ׃פ\rb* \rb dominion|חֲלָק֙\rb* \rb west|בַּעֲבַ֣ר\rb* \rb of the Euphrates|נַהֲרָ֔א\rb*.
\s1 The Decree of Artaxerxes
\p \v 17 \rb Then the king|מַלְכָּ֗א\rb* \rb sent|שְׁלַ֣ח\rb* \rb this reply|פִּתְגָמָ֞א\rb*:
\p \rb To|עַל־\rb* \rb Rehum|רְח֤וּם\rb* \rb the commander|בְּעֵל־\rb*\rb |טְעֵם֙\rb*, \rb Shimshai|וְשִׁמְשַׁ֣י\rb* \rb the scribe|סָֽפְרָ֔א\rb*, \rb and the rest|וּשְׁאָר֙\rb* \rb of your associates|כְּנָוָ֣תְה֔וֹן\rb*\rb |דִּ֥י\rb* \rb living|יָתְבִ֖ין\rb* \rb in Samaria|בְּשָֽׁמְרָ֑יִן\rb* \rb and elsewhere|וּשְׁאָ֧ר\rb* \rb in the region west|עֲבַֽר־\rb* \rb of the Euphrates|נַהֲרָ֛ה\rb*:
\p \rb Greetings|שְׁלָ֖ם\rb*.\rb |וּכְעֶֽת׃ס\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb The letter|נִשְׁתְּוָנָ֕א\rb*\rb |דִּ֥י\rb* \rb you sent|שְׁלַחְתּ֖וּן\rb* \rb us|עֲלֶ֑ינָא\rb* \rb has been translated|מְפָרַ֥שׁ\rb* \rb and read|קֱרִ֖י\rb* \rb in my presence|קָדָמָֽי׃\rb*. \v 19 \rb |וּמִנִּי֮\rb* \rb I issued|שִׂ֣ים\rb* \rb a decree|טְעֵם֒\rb*, \rb and a search was conducted|וּבַקַּ֣רוּ\rb*. \rb It was discovered|וְהַשְׁכַּ֔חוּ\rb* \rb that|דִּ֚י\rb* \rb this|דָ֔ךְ\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb city|קִרְיְתָ֣א\rb* \rb has revolted|מִֽתְנַשְּׂאָ֑ה\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb kings|מַלְכִ֖ין\rb* \rb from ancient|עָֽלְמָ֔א\rb* \rb times|יוֹמָת֙\rb*, \rb engaging in rebellion|וּמְרַ֥ד\rb* \rb and sedition|וְאֶשְׁתַּדּ֖וּר\rb*\rb |מִתְעֲבֶד־\rb*. \v 20 \rb And mighty|תַּקִּיפִ֗ין\rb*\rb |הֲווֹ֙\rb* \rb kings|וּמַלְכִ֣ין\rb* \rb have ruled over|עַל־\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְר֣וּשְׁלֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and exercised authority|וְשַׁ֨לִּיטִ֔ין\rb* \rb over the whole|בְּכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb region west|עֲבַ֣ר\rb* \rb of the Euphrates|נַהֲרָ֑ה\rb*; \rb and tribute|וּמִדָּ֥ה\rb*, \rb duty|בְל֛וֹ\rb*, \rb and toll|וַהֲלָ֖ךְ\rb* \rb were paid|מִתְיְהֵ֥ב\rb* \rb to them|לְהֽוֹן׃\rb*.
\p \v 21 \rb Now, therefore|כְּעַן֙\rb*, \rb issue|שִׂ֣ימוּ\rb* \rb an order|טְּעֵ֔ם\rb* \rb for these|אִלֵּ֑ךְ\rb* \rb men|גֻּבְרַיָּ֣א\rb* \rb to stop|לְבַטָּלָ֖א\rb*, \rb so that this|דָךְ֙\rb* \rb city|וְקִרְיְתָ֥א\rb* \rb will not|לָ֣א\rb* \rb be rebuilt|תִתְבְּנֵ֔א\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb I|מִנִּ֖י\rb* \rb so order|טַעְמָ֥א\rb*\rb |יִתְּשָֽׂם׃\rb*. \v 22 \rb See that you|וּזְהִירִ֥ין\rb*\rb |הֱו֛וֹ\rb* \rb do not neglect|שָׁל֖וּ\rb*\rb |לְמֶעְבַּ֣ד\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb this matter|דְּנָ֑ה\rb*. \rb Why|לְמָה֙\rb* \rb allow this threat|חֲבָלָ֔א\rb* \rb to increase|יִשְׂגֵּ֣א\rb* \rb and the royal|מַלְכִֽין׃ס\rb* \rb interests to suffer|לְהַנְזָקַ֖ת\rb*?
\p \v 23 \rb When|אֱדַ֗יִן\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb*\rb |דִּ֞י\rb* \rb the text|פַּרְשֶׁ֤גֶן\rb* \rb of the letter|נִשְׁתְּוָנָא֙\rb* \rb from King|מַלְכָּ֔א\rb* \rb Artaxerxes|אַרְתַּחְשַׁשְׂתָּא\rb* \rb was read|קֱרִ֧י\rb* \rb to|קֳדָם־\rb* \rb Rehum|רְח֛וּם\rb*, \rb Shimshai|וְשִׁמְשַׁ֥י\rb* \rb the scribe|סָפְרָ֖א\rb*, \rb and their associates|וּכְנָוָתְה֑וֹן\rb*, \rb they went|אֲזַ֨לוּ\rb* \rb immediately|בִבְהִיל֤וּ\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the Jews|יְה֣וּדָיֵ֔א\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|לִירֽוּשְׁלֶם֙\rb* \rb and forcibly|בְּאֶדְרָ֥ע\rb*\rb |וְחָֽיִל׃ס\rb* \rb stopped|וּבַטִּ֥לוּ\rb* \rb them|הִמּ֖וֹ\rb*.
\p \v 24 \rb Thus|בֵּאדַ֗יִן\rb* \rb the construction|עֲבִידַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of God|אֱלָהָ֔א\rb*\rb |דִּ֖י\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשְׁלֶ֑ם\rb* \rb ceased|בְּטֵלַת֙\rb*, \rb and it remained|וַהֲוָת֙\rb* \rb at a standstill|בָּֽטְלָ֔א\rb* \rb until|עַ֚ד\rb* \rb the second|תַּרְתֵּ֔ין\rb* \rb year|שְׁנַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the reign|לְמַלְכ֖וּת\rb* \rb of Darius|דָּרְיָ֥וֶשׁ\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Persia|פָּרָֽס׃פ\rb*.
\c 5
\s1 Temple Rebuilding Resumes
\p \v 1 \rb Later, the prophets|נְבִיאָה\rb* \rb Haggai|חַגַּ֣י\rb* \rb and Zechariah|וּזְכַרְיָ֤ה\rb* \rb son|בַר־\rb* \rb of Iddo|עִדּוֹא֙\rb* \rb prophesied|וְהִתְנַבִּ֞י\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the Jews|יְה֣וּדָיֵ֔א\rb*\rb |דִּ֥י\rb* \rb in Judah|בִיה֖וּד\rb* \rb and Jerusalem|וּבִירוּשְׁלֶ֑ם\rb* \rb in the name|בְּשֻׁ֛ם\rb* \rb of the God|אֱלָ֥הּ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*, \rb who was over them|עֲלֵיהֽוֹן׃ס\rb*. \v 2 \rb Then|בֵּאדַ֡יִן\rb* \rb Zerubbabel|זְרֻבָּבֶ֤ל\rb* \rb son|בַּר־\rb* \rb of Shealtiel|שְׁאַלְתִּיאֵל֙\rb* \rb and Jeshua|וְיֵשׁ֣וּעַ\rb* \rb son|בַּר־\rb* \rb of Jozadak|יֽוֹצָדָ֔ק\rb*\f + \fr 5:2 \fqa Jozadak \ft is a variant of \fqa Jehozadak\ft ; see 1 Chronicles 6:14.\f* \rb rose up|קָ֠מוּ\rb* \rb and began|וְשָׁרִ֣יו\rb* \rb to rebuild|לְמִבְנֵ֔א\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of God|אֱלָהָ֖א\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִירֽוּשְׁלֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb And the prophets|נְבִיאַיָּא\rb*\rb |דִֽי־\rb* \rb of|דִּ֣י\rb* \rb God|אֱלָהָ֖א\rb* \rb were with them|וְעִמְּה֛וֹן\rb*, \rb helping|מְסָעֲדִ֥ין\rb* \rb them|לְהֽוֹן׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb At that time|זִמְנָא֩\rb* \rb Tattenai|תַּ֠תְּנַי\rb* \rb the governor|פַּחַ֧ת\rb* \rb of the region west|עֲבַֽר־\rb* \rb of the Euphrates|נַהֲרָ֛ה\rb*,\f + \fr 5:3 \ft Aramaic \fqa the governor beyond the River\ft ; also in verse 6\f*\rb |וּשְׁתַ֥ר\rb* \rb Shethar-bozenai|בּוֹזְנַ֖י\rb*, \rb and their associates|וּכְנָוָתְה֑וֹן\rb*\rb |וְכֵן֙\rb* \rb went|אֲתָ֨א\rb* \rb to the Jews|עֲלֵיה֜וֹן\rb* \rb and asked|אָמְרִ֣ין\rb*, “\rb Who|מַן־\rb* \rb authorized you|שָׂ֨ם\rb*\rb |טְעֵ֗ם\rb* \rb to rebuild|לִבְּנֵ֔א\rb* \rb this|דְנָה֙\rb* \rb temple|בַּיְתָ֤א\rb* \rb and restore|לְשַׁכְלָלָֽה׃ס\rb* \rb this|דְנָ֖ה\rb* \rb structure|וְאֻשַּׁרְנָ֥א\rb*?”
\p \v 4 \rb They also|אֱדַ֥יִן\rb*\rb |כְּנֵ֖מָא\rb* \rb asked|אֲמַ֣רְנָא\rb*,\f + \fr 5:4 \ft LXX and Syriac; Aramaic \fqa Then we told them,\f* “\rb What|מַן־\rb* \rb are|אִנּוּן֙\rb* \rb the names|שְׁמָהָ֣ת\rb* \rb of the men|גֻּבְרַיָּ֔א\rb* \rb who|דִּֽי־\rb* \rb are constructing|בָּנַֽיִן׃\rb* \rb this|דְנָ֥ה\rb* \rb building|בִנְיָנָ֖א\rb*?”
\p \v 5 \rb But the eye|וְעֵ֣ין\rb* \rb of their God|אֱלָהֲהֹ֗ם\rb* \rb was|הֲוָת֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the elders|שָׂבֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the Jews|יְהוּדָיֵ֔א\rb*, \rb so that they were not|וְלָא־\rb* \rb stopped|בַטִּ֣לוּ\rb*\rb |הִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb a report|טַעְמָ֖א\rb* \rb was sent|יְהָ֑ךְ\rb* \rb to Darius|לְדָרְיָ֣וֶשׁ\rb* \rb and|וֶאֱדַ֛יִן\rb* \rb written instructions|נִשְׁתְּוָנָ֖א\rb* \rb about|עַל־\rb* \rb this matter|דְּנָֽה׃פ\rb* \rb were returned|יְתִיב֥וּן\rb*.
\s1 Tattenai’s Letter to Darius
\p \v 6 \rb This is the text|פַּרְשֶׁ֣גֶן\rb* \rb of the letter|אִ֠גַּרְתָּא\rb* \rb that|דִּֽי־\rb* \rb Tattenai|תַּתְּנַ֣י׀\rb* \rb the governor|פַּחַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the region west|עֲבַֽר־\rb* \rb of the Euphrates|נַהֲרָ֗ה\rb*,\rb |וּשְׁתַ֤ר\rb* \rb Shethar-bozenai|בּוֹזְנַי֙\rb*, \rb and their associates|וּכְנָ֣וָתֵ֔הּ\rb*, \rb the officials|אֲפַ֨רְסְכָיֵ֔א\rb*\rb |דִּ֖י\rb* \rb in the region|בַּעֲבַ֣ר\rb*,\rb |נַהֲרָ֑ה\rb* \rb sent|שְׁלַ֞ח\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb King|מַלְכָּֽא׃\rb* \rb Darius|דָּרְיָ֖וֶשׁ\rb*. \v 7 \rb The report|פִּתְגָמָ֖א\rb* \rb they sent|שְׁלַ֣חוּ\rb* \rb him|עֲל֑וֹהִי\rb* \rb read as follows|כְּתִ֣יב\rb*\rb |בְּגַוֵּ֔הּ\rb*\rb |וְכִדְנָה֙\rb*:
\p \rb To King|מַלְכָּ֖א\rb* \rb Darius|לְדָרְיָ֥וֶשׁ\rb*:
\p \rb All|כֹֽלָּא׃ס\rb* \rb peace|שְׁלָמָ֥א\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb Let it be|לֶהֱוֵ֣א\rb* \rb known|יְדִ֣יעַ׀\rb* \rb to the king|לְמַלְכָּ֗א\rb* \rb that|דִּֽי־\rb* \rb we went|אֲזַ֜לְנָא\rb* \rb into the province|מְדִֽינְתָּא֙\rb* \rb of Judah|לִיה֤וּד\rb*, \rb to the house|לְבֵית֙\rb* \rb of the great|רַבָּ֔א\rb* \rb God|אֱלָהָ֣א\rb*. \rb The people|וְה֤וּא\rb* \rb are rebuilding it|מִתְבְּנֵא֙\rb* \rb with large stones|אֶ֣בֶן\rb*\rb |גְּלָ֔ל\rb* \rb and placing|מִתְּשָׂ֣ם\rb* \rb timbers|וְאָ֖ע\rb* \rb in the walls|בְּכֻתְלַיָּ֑א\rb*. \rb This|דָ֛ךְ\rb* \rb work|וַעֲבִ֥ידְתָּא\rb* \rb is being carried out|מִתְעַבְדָ֖א\rb* \rb diligently|אָסְפַּ֥רְנָא\rb* \rb and is prospering|וּמַצְלַ֥ח\rb* \rb in their hands|בְּיֶדְהֹֽם׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb So|אֱדַ֗יִן\rb* \rb we questioned|שְׁאֵ֙לְנָא֙\rb* \rb the|אִלֵּ֔ךְ\rb*\rb |כְּנֵ֖מָא\rb* \rb elders|לְשָׂבַיָּ֣א\rb* \rb and asked|אֲמַ֣רְנָא\rb*, “\rb Who|מַן־\rb* \rb authorized|שָׂ֨ם\rb*\rb |טְעֵ֗ם\rb* \rb you|לְכֹ֜ם\rb* \rb to rebuild|לְמִבְנְיָ֔ה\rb* \rb this|דְנָה֙\rb* \rb temple|בַּיְתָ֤א\rb* \rb and restore|לְשַׁכְלָלָֽה׃\rb* \rb this|דְנָ֖ה\rb* \rb structure|וְאֻשַּׁרְנָ֥א\rb*?”
\p \v 10 \rb We also|וְאַ֧ף\rb* \rb asked for|שְׁאֵ֥לְנָא\rb* \rb their|לְּהֹ֖ם\rb* \rb names|שְׁמָהָתְהֹ֛ם\rb*, \rb so that|דִּ֛י\rb* \rb we could write down|נִכְתֻּ֥ב\rb* \rb the names|שֻׁם־\rb* \rb of their leaders|גֻּבְרַיָּ֖א\rb*\rb |דִּ֥י\rb*\rb |בְרָאשֵׁיהֹֽם׃ס\rb*\f + \fr 5:10 \ft Aramaic \fqa the names of the men at their heads\f* \rb for your information|לְהוֹדָעוּתָ֑ךְ\rb*.
\p \v 11 \rb And this|וּכְנֵ֥מָא\rb* \rb is the answer|פִתְגָמָ֖א\rb* \rb they returned|הֲתִיב֣וּנָא\rb*\rb |לְמֵמַ֑ר\rb*:
\p “\rb We|אֲנַ֣חְנָא\rb* \rb are|הִמּ֡וֹ\rb* \rb servants|עַבְדוֹהִי֩\rb* \rb of the God|אֱלָ֨הּ\rb* \rb of heaven|שְׁמַיָּ֜א\rb* \rb and earth|וְאַרְעָ֗א\rb*, \rb and we are rebuilding|וּבָנַ֤יִן\rb* \rb the temple|בַּיְתָא֙\rb* \rb that|דִּֽי־\rb* \rb was|הֲוָ֨א\rb* \rb built|בְנֵ֜ה\rb* \rb many|שַׂגִּיאָ֔ן\rb* \rb years|שְׁנִ֣ין\rb* \rb ago|מִקַּדְמַ֤ת\rb*,\rb |דְּנָה֙\rb* \rb which a great|רַ֔ב\rb* \rb king|וּמֶ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel|לְיִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb built|בְּנָ֖הִי\rb* \rb and completed|וְשַׁכְלְלֵֽהּ׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb But|לָהֵ֗ן\rb* \rb since|מִן־\rb*\rb |דִּ֨י\rb* \rb our fathers|אֲבָהֳתַ֙נָא֙\rb* \rb angered|הַרְגִּ֤זוּ\rb* \rb the God|לֶאֱלָ֣הּ\rb* \rb of heaven|שְׁמַיָּ֔א\rb*, \rb He delivered|יְהַ֣ב\rb* \rb them|הִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb into the hand|בְּיַ֛ד\rb* \rb of Nebuchadnezzar|נְבוּכַדְנֶצַּ֥ר\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֖ל\rb*, \rb the Chaldean|כַּסְדָּיָא\rb* \rb who destroyed|סַתְרֵ֔הּ\rb* \rb this|דְנָה֙\rb* \rb temple|וּבַיְתָ֤ה\rb* \rb and carried away|הַגְלִ֥י\rb* \rb the people|וְעַמָּ֖ה\rb* \rb to Babylon|לְבָבֶֽל׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb In the first|חֲדָ֔ה\rb* \rb year of his reign|בִּשְׁנַ֣ת\rb*, \rb however|בְּרַם֙\rb*, \rb Cyrus|לְכ֥וֹרֶשׁ\rb* \rb king|מַלְכָּ֖א\rb* \rb of|דִּ֣י\rb* \rb Babylon|בָבֶ֑ל\rb*\rb |כּ֤וֹרֶשׁ\rb*\rb |מַלְכָּא֙\rb* \rb issued|שָׂ֣ם\rb* \rb a decree|טְעֵ֔ם\rb* \rb to rebuild|לִבְּנֵֽא׃\rb* \rb this|דְנָ֖ה\rb* \rb house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of God|אֱלָהָ֥א\rb*. \v 14 \rb He also|וְ֠אַף\rb* \rb removed|הַנְפֵּ֨ק\rb*\rb |הִמּ֜וֹ\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the temple|הֵֽיכְלָא֙\rb*\f + \fr 5:14 \ft Or \fqa palace\f* \rb of|דִּ֣י\rb* \rb Babylon|בָבֶ֔ל\rb* \rb the gold|דַהֲבָ֣ה\rb* \rb and silver|וְכַסְפָּא֒\rb* \rb articles|מָאנַיָּ֣א\rb* \rb belonging to|דִֽי־\rb* \rb the house|בֵית־\rb* \rb of God|אֱלָהָא֮\rb*, \rb which|דִּ֣י\rb*\rb |דִּ֣י\rb* \rb Nebuchadnezzar|נְבוּכַדְנֶצַּ֗ר\rb* \rb had taken|הַנְפֵּק֙\rb* \rb and carried|וְהֵיבֵ֣ל\rb*\rb |הִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb there|לְהֵיכְלָ֖א\rb*\rb |דִּ֣י\rb*\rb |בָבֶ֑ל\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the temple|הֵֽיכְלָא֙\rb*\rb |דִּ֣י\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִֽירוּשְׁלֶ֔ם\rb*. \rb King|מַלְכָּ֗א\rb* \rb Cyrus|כּ֣וֹרֶשׁ\rb* \rb gave these articles|וִיהִ֙יבוּ֙\rb* \rb to a man named|שְׁמֵ֔הּ\rb*\rb |דִּ֥י\rb* \rb Sheshbazzar|לְשֵׁשְׁבַּצַּ֣ר\rb*, \rb whom he appointed|שָׂמֵֽהּ׃\rb* \rb governor|פֶחָ֖ה\rb* \v 15 \rb and instructed|וַאֲמַר־\rb*, ‘\rb Take|שֵׂ֚א\rb*\rb |אֵֽזֶל־\rb* \rb these|אֵלֶּה\rb* \rb articles|מָֽאנַיָּ֔א\rb*, \rb put|אֲחֵ֣ת\rb* \rb them|הִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb in the temple|בְּהֵיכְלָ֖א\rb*\rb |דִּ֣י\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִירוּשְׁלֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb and let the house|וּבֵ֥ית\rb* \rb of God|אֱלָהָ֖א\rb* \rb be rebuilt|יִתְבְּנֵ֥א\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb its original site|אַתְרֵֽהּ׃ס\rb*.’
\p \v 16 \rb So|אֱדַ֙יִן֙\rb* \rb this|דֵּ֔ךְ\rb* \rb Sheshbazzar|שֵׁשְׁבַּצַּ֣ר\rb* \rb came|אֲתָ֗א\rb* \rb and laid|יְהַ֧ב\rb* \rb the foundation|אֻשַּׁיָּ֛א\rb* \rb of|דִּי־\rb* \rb the house|בֵ֥ית\rb* \rb of God|אֱלָהָ֖א\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִירוּשְׁלֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb and from|וּמִן־\rb* \rb that time|אֱדַ֧יִן\rb* \rb until|וְעַד־\rb* \rb now|כְּעַ֛ן\rb* \rb it has been under construction|מִתְבְּנֵ֖א\rb*, \rb but it has not yet|וְלָ֥א\rb* \rb been completed|שְׁלִֽם׃\rb*.”
\p \v 17 \rb Now, therefore,|וּכְעַ֞ן\rb* \rb if|הֵ֧ן\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb it pleases|טָ֗ב\rb* \rb the king|מַלְכָּ֣א\rb*, \rb let a search be made|יִ֠תְבַּקַּר\rb* \rb of the royal|דִּי־\rb*\rb |מַלְכָּ֣א\rb*\rb |תַמָּה֮\rb* \rb archives|בְּבֵ֨ית\rb*\rb |גִּנְזַיָּ֜א\rb* \rb in Babylon|בְּבָבֶל֒\rb* \rb to see if|הֵ֣ן\rb*\rb |אִיתַ֗י\rb*\rb |דִּֽי־\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb King|מַלְכָּא֙\rb* \rb Cyrus|כּ֤וֹרֶשׁ\rb* \rb did indeed issue|שִׂ֣ים\rb* \rb a decree|טְעֵ֔ם\rb* \rb to rebuild|לְמִבְנֵ֛א\rb* \rb the|דֵ֖ךְ\rb* \rb house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of God|אֱלָהָ֥א\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשְׁלֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb Then let the king|מַלְכָּ֛א\rb* \rb send|יִשְׁלַ֥ח\rb* \rb us|עֲלֶֽינָא׃ס\rb* \rb his decision|וּרְע֥וּת\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb this matter|דְּנָ֖ה\rb*.
\c 6
\s1 The Decree of Darius
\p \v 1 \rb Thus|בֵּאדַ֛יִן\rb* \rb King|מַלְכָּ֖א\rb* \rb Darius|דָּרְיָ֥וֶשׁ\rb* \rb ordered|שָׂ֣ם\rb*\rb |טְעֵ֑ם\rb* \rb a search|וּבַקַּ֣רוּ׀\rb* \rb of the archives|בְּבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb stored|מְהַחֲתִ֥ין\rb*\rb |סִפְרַיָּ֗א\rb*\rb |דִּ֧י\rb* \rb in the treasury|גִנְזַיָּ֛א\rb* \rb of Babylon|בְּבָבֶֽל׃\rb*\rb |תַּמָּ֖ה\rb*. \v 2 \rb And a scroll|מְגִלָּ֣ה\rb* \rb was found|וְהִשְׁתְּכַ֣ח\rb* \rb in the fortress|בְּבִֽירְתָ֛א\rb*\rb |דִּ֛י\rb* \rb of Ecbatana|בְּאַחְמְתָ֗א\rb*, \rb in the province|מְדִינְתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb of Media|בְּמָדַ֥י\rb*, \rb with the following|וְכֵן־\rb* \rb written|כְּתִ֥יב\rb* \rb on it|בְּגַוַּ֖הּ\rb*:
\p \rb Memorandum|דִּכְרוֹנָֽה׃פ\rb*:
\p \v 3 \rb In the first|חֲדָ֜ה\rb* \rb year|בִּשְׁנַ֨ת\rb* \rb of King|מַלְכָּ֗א\rb* \rb Cyrus|לְכ֣וֹרֶשׁ\rb*, \rb he|כּ֣וֹרֶשׁ\rb*\rb |מַלְכָּא֮\rb* \rb issued|שָׂ֣ם\rb* \rb a decree concerning|טְעֵם֒\rb* \rb the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of God|אֱלָהָ֤א\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִֽירוּשְׁלֶם֙\rb*:
\p \rb Let the house|בַּיְתָ֣א\rb* \rb be rebuilt|יִתְבְּנֵ֔א\rb* \rb as a place|אֲתַר֙\rb* \rb for|דִּֽי־\rb* \rb offering|דָבְחִ֣ין\rb* \rb sacrifices|דִּבְחִ֔ין\rb*, \rb and let its foundations|וְאֻשּׁ֖וֹהִי\rb* \rb be firmly laid|מְסֽוֹבְלִ֑ין\rb*. \rb It is to be sixty|שִׁתִּ֔ין\rb* \rb cubits|אַמִּ֣ין\rb* \rb high|רוּמֵהּ֙\rb* \rb and sixty|שִׁתִּֽין׃\rb* \rb cubits|אַמִּ֥ין\rb* \rb wide|פְּתָיֵ֖הּ\rb*,\f + \fr 6:3 \ft The house was to be approximately 90 feet or 27.4 meters in height and width; Syriac (see also 1 Kings 6:2) \fqa It is to be sixty cubits long, twenty cubits wide, and thirty cubits high\ft .\f* \v 4 \rb with three|תְּלָתָ֔א\rb*\rb |וְנִדְבָּ֖ךְ\rb* \rb layers|נִדְבָּכִ֞ין\rb* \rb of|דִּי־\rb* \rb cut stones|אֶ֤בֶן\rb*\rb |גְּלָל֙\rb* \rb and one|חֲדַ֑ת\rb* \rb of|דִּי־\rb* \rb timbers|אָ֣ע\rb*. \rb The costs|וְנִ֨פְקְתָ֔א\rb* \rb are to be paid|תִּתְיְהִֽב׃\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the royal|מַלְכָּ֖א\rb* \rb treasury|בֵּ֥ית\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb Furthermore|וְ֠אַף\rb*, \rb the gold|דַהֲבָ֣ה\rb* \rb and silver|וְכַסְפָּא֒\rb*\rb |דִּ֣י\rb* \rb articles|מָאנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the house|בֵית־\rb* \rb of God|אֱלָהָא֮\rb*, \rb which|דִּ֣י\rb* \rb Nebuchadnezzar|נְבֽוּכַדְנֶצַּ֗ר\rb* \rb took|הַנְפֵּ֛ק\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the temple|הֵיכְלָ֥א\rb*\rb |דִי־\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִירוּשְׁלֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and carried|וְהֵיבֵ֣ל\rb* \rb to Babylon|לְבָבֶ֑ל\rb*, \rb must also be returned|יַהֲתִיב֗וּן\rb*\rb |וִ֠יהָךְ\rb* \rb to the temple|לְהֵיכְלָ֤א\rb*\rb |דִי־\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִירֽוּשְׁלֶם֙\rb*\rb |לְאַתְרֵ֔הּ\rb* \rb and deposited|וְתַחֵ֖ת\rb* \rb in the house|בְּבֵ֥ית\rb* \rb of God|אֱלָהָֽא׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb Therefore Darius decreed|כְּעַ֡ן\rb*:
\p \rb To Tattenai|תַּ֠תְּנַי\rb* \rb governor|פַּחַ֨ת\rb* \rb of the region west|עֲבַֽר־\rb* \rb of the Euphrates|נַהֲרָ֜ה\rb*,\f + \fr 6:6 \ft Aramaic \fqa governor beyond the River\ft ; similarly in verses 8 and 13\f*\rb |שְׁתַ֤ר\rb* \rb Shethar-bozenai|בּוֹזְנַי֙\rb*, \rb and your associates|וּכְנָוָ֣תְה֔וֹן\rb* \rb and officials|אֲפַרְסְכָיֵ֔א\rb*\rb |דִּ֖י\rb* \rb in the region|בַּעֲבַ֣ר\rb*\rb |נַהֲרָ֑ה\rb*:
\p \rb You must stay|הֲו֖וֹ\rb* \rb away|רַחִיקִ֥ין\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb that place|תַּמָּֽה׃\rb*! \v 7 \rb Leave this work|לַעֲבִידַ֖ת\rb*\rb |דֵ֑ךְ\rb* \rb on the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of God|אֱלָהָ֣א\rb* \rb alone|שְׁבֻ֕קוּ\rb*. \rb Let the governor|פַּחַ֤ת\rb* \rb and elders|וּלְשָׂבֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יְהוּדָיֵ֔א\rb* \rb of the Jews|יְהוּדָיֵא֙\rb* \rb rebuild|יִבְנ֥וֹן\rb* \rb this|דֵ֖ךְ\rb* \rb house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of God|אֱלָהָ֥א\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb its original site|אַתְרֵֽהּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb I hereby|וּמִנִּי֮\rb*\rb |שִׂ֣ים\rb* \rb decree|טְעֵם֒\rb* \rb what|לְמָ֣א\rb*\rb |דִֽי־\rb* \rb you must do|תַֽעַבְד֗וּן\rb* \rb for|עִם־\rb* \rb these|אִלֵּ֔ךְ\rb* \rb elders|שָׂבֵ֤י\rb* \rb of the Jews|יְהוּדָיֵא֙\rb* \rb who are rebuilding|לְמִבְנֵ֖א\rb* \rb this|דֵ֑ךְ\rb* \rb house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of God|אֱלָהָ֣א\rb*:
\p \rb The cost|נִפְקְתָ֛א\rb* \rb is to be|תֶּהֱוֵ֧א\rb* \rb paid|מִֽתְיַהֲבָ֛א\rb* \rb in full|אָסְפַּ֗רְנָא\rb* \rb to these|אִלֵּ֖ךְ\rb* \rb men|לְגֻבְרַיָּ֥א\rb* \rb from the royal|מַלְכָּ֗א\rb* \rb treasury|וּמִנִּכְסֵ֣י\rb* \rb out of|דִּ֚י\rb* \rb the taxes|מִדַּת֙\rb* \rb of the provinces west|עֲבַ֣ר\rb* \rb of the Euphrates|נַהֲרָ֔ה\rb*, \rb so that|דִּי־\rb* \rb the work will not|לָ֥א\rb* \rb be hindered|לְבַטָּלָֽא׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb Whatever|וּמָ֣ה\rb* \rb is needed|חַשְׁחָ֡ן\rb*— \rb young|וּבְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb bulls|תוֹרִ֣ין\rb*, \rb rams|וְדִכְרִ֣ין\rb*, \rb and lambs|וְאִמְּרִ֣ין׀\rb* \rb for burnt offerings|לַעֲלָוָ֣ן׀\rb* \rb to the God|לֶאֱלָ֪הּ\rb* \rb of heaven|שְׁמַיָּ֟א\rb*, \rb as well as wheat|חִנְטִ֞ין\rb*, \rb salt|מְלַ֣ח׀\rb*, \rb wine|חֲמַ֣ר\rb*, \rb and oil|וּמְשַׁ֗ח\rb*, \rb as requested|כְּמֵאמַ֨ר\rb* \rb by the priests|כָּהֲנַיָּ֤א\rb*\rb |דִי־\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִירֽוּשְׁלֶם֙\rb*— \rb must be|לֶהֱוֵ֨א\rb* \rb given|מִתְיְהֵ֥ב\rb* \rb to them|לְהֹ֛ם\rb* \rb daily|י֥וֹם׀\rb*\rb |בְּי֖וֹם\rb*\rb |דִּי־\rb* \rb without|לָ֥א\rb* \rb fail|שָׁלֽוּ׃\rb*. \v 10 \rb Then|דִּֽי־\rb* \rb they will be able|לֶהֱוֺ֧ן\rb* \rb to offer sacrifices|מְהַקְרְבִ֛ין\rb* \rb of a sweet aroma|נִיחוֹחִ֖ין\rb* \rb to the God|לֶאֱלָ֣הּ\rb* \rb of heaven|שְׁמַיָּ֑א\rb* \rb and to pray|וּמְצַלַּ֕יִן\rb* \rb for the lives|לְחַיֵּ֥י\rb* \rb of the king|מַלְכָּ֖א\rb* \rb and his sons|וּבְנֽוֹהִי׃\rb*.
\p \v 11 \rb I also|וּמִנִּי֮\rb* \rb decree|שִׂ֣ים\rb*\rb |טְעֵם֒\rb* \rb that|דִּ֣י\rb* \rb if any|כָל־\rb* \rb man|אֱנָ֗שׁ\rb*\rb |דִּ֤י\rb* \rb interferes|יְהַשְׁנֵא֙\rb* \rb with this|דְנָ֔ה\rb* \rb directive|פִּתְגָמָ֣א\rb*, \rb a beam|אָע֙\rb* \rb is to be torn|יִתְנְסַ֥ח\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb his house|בַּיְתֵ֔הּ\rb* \rb and raised up|וּזְקִ֖יף\rb*, \rb and he is to be impaled|יִתְמְחֵ֣א\rb* \rb on it|עֲלֹ֑הִי\rb*. \rb And his own house|וּבַיְתֵ֛הּ\rb* \rb shall be made|יִתְעֲבֵ֖ד\rb* \rb a pile of rubble|נְוָל֥וּ\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb this offense|דְּנָֽה׃\rb*.\f + \fr 6:11 \ft Literally \fqa shall be made a dunghill because of this\f* \v 12 \rb May God|וֵֽאלָהָ֞א\rb*, \rb who|דִּ֣י\rb* \rb has caused His Name|שְׁמֵ֣הּ\rb* \rb to dwell|שַׁכִּ֧ן\rb* \rb there|תַּמָּ֗ה\rb*, \rb overthrow|יְמַגַּ֞ר\rb* \rb any|כָּל־\rb* \rb king|מֶ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb or people|וְעַם֙\rb* \rb who|דִּ֣י׀\rb* \rb lifts|יִשְׁלַ֣ח\rb* \rb a hand|יְדֵ֗הּ\rb* \rb to alter this decree|לְהַשְׁנָיָ֛ה\rb* \rb or to destroy|לְחַבָּלָ֛ה\rb* \rb this|דֵ֖ךְ\rb* \rb house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of God|אֱלָהָ֥א\rb*\rb |דִּ֣י\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִירוּשְׁלֶ֑ם\rb*.
\p \rb I|אֲנָ֤ה\rb*, \rb Darius|דָרְיָ֙וֶשׁ֙\rb*, \rb have issued|שָׂ֣מֶת\rb* \rb the decree|טְעֵ֔ם\rb*. \rb Let it be carried out|יִתְעֲבִֽד׃פ\rb* \rb with diligence|אָסְפַּ֖רְנָא\rb*.
\s1 The Temple Completed
\p \v 13 \rb In response|אֱ֠דַיִן\rb*, \rb Tattenai|תַּתְּנַ֞י\rb* \rb the governor|פַּחַ֧ת\rb* \rb of the region west|עֲבַֽר־\rb* \rb of the Euphrates|נַהֲרָ֛ה\rb*,\rb |שְׁתַ֥ר\rb* \rb Shethar-bozenai|בּוֹזְנַ֖י\rb*, \rb and their associates|וּכְנָוָתְה֑וֹן\rb*\rb |לָקֳבֵ֗ל\rb* \rb diligently|אָסְפַּ֥רְנָא\rb* \rb carried out|עֲבַֽדוּ׃\rb* \rb what|דִּֽי־\rb* \rb King|מַלְכָּ֛א\rb*\rb |כְּנֵ֖מָא\rb* \rb Darius|דָּרְיָ֧וֶשׁ\rb* \rb had decreed|שְׁלַ֞ח\rb*. \v 14 \rb So the Jewish|יְהוּדָיֵא֙\rb* \rb elders|וְשָׂבֵ֤י\rb* \rb built|בָּנַ֣יִן\rb* \rb and prospered|וּמַצְלְחִ֔ין\rb* \rb through the prophesying|בִּנְבוּאַת֙\rb* \rb of Haggai|חַגַּ֣י\rb* \rb the prophet|נְבִיאָה\rb* \rb and Zechariah|וּזְכַרְיָ֖ה\rb* \rb son|בַּר־\rb* \rb of Iddo|עִדּ֑וֹא\rb*.
\p \rb They finished|וְשַׁכְלִ֗לוּ\rb* \rb building|וּבְנ֣וֹ\rb* \rb according to|מִן־\rb* \rb the command|טַ֙עַם֙\rb* \rb of the God|אֱלָ֣הּ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb and the decrees|וּמִטְּעֵם֙\rb* \rb of Cyrus|כּ֣וֹרֶשׁ\rb*, \rb Darius|וְדָרְיָ֔וֶשׁ\rb*, \rb and Artaxerxes|וְאַרְתַּחְשַׁ֖שְׂתְּא\rb*, \rb kings|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Persia|פָּרָֽס׃\rb*. \v 15 \rb And this|דְנָ֔ה\rb* \rb temple|בַּיְתָ֣ה\rb* \rb was completed|וְשֵׁיצִיא֙\rb* \rb on|עַ֛ד\rb* \rb the third|תְּלָתָ֖ה\rb* \rb day|י֥וֹם\rb* \rb of the month|לִירַ֣ח\rb* \rb of Adar|אֲדָ֑ר\rb*,\f + \fr 6:15 \fqa Adar \ft is the twelfth month of the Hebrew lunar calendar, usually occurring within the months of February and March.\f*\rb |דִּי־\rb*\rb |הִ֣יא\rb* \rb in the sixth|שֵׁ֔ת\rb* \rb year|שְׁנַת־\rb* \rb of the reign|לְמַלְכ֖וּת\rb* \rb of King|מַלְכָּֽא׃פ\rb* \rb Darius|דָּרְיָ֥וֶשׁ\rb*.
\s1 Dedication of the Temple
\p \v 16 \rb Then the people|בְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִ֠שְׂרָאֵל\rb* — \rb the priests|כָּהֲנַיָּ֨א\rb*, \rb the Levites|וְלֵוָיֵ֜א\rb*, \rb and the rest|וּשְׁאָ֣ר\rb* \rb of the exiles|בְּנֵי־\rb*\rb |גָלוּתָ֗א\rb* — \rb celebrated|וַעֲבַ֣דוּ\rb* \rb the dedication|חֲנֻכַּ֛ת\rb* \rb of the|דְנָ֖ה\rb* \rb house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of God|אֱלָהָ֥א\rb* \rb with joy|בְּחֶדְוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 17 \rb For the|דְנָה֒\rb* \rb dedication|לַחֲנֻכַּת֮\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of God|אֱלָהָ֣א\rb* \rb they offered|וְהַקְרִ֗בוּ\rb* \rb a hundred|מְאָ֔ה\rb* \rb bulls|תּוֹרִ֣ין\rb*, \rb two hundred|מָאתַ֔יִן\rb* \rb rams|דִּכְרִ֣ין\rb*, \rb four|אַרְבַּ֣ע\rb* \rb hundred|מְאָ֑ה\rb* \rb lambs|אִמְּרִ֖ין\rb*, \rb and a sin offering|לְחַטָּיָא\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb of twelve|תְּרֵֽי־\rb*\rb |עֲשַׂ֔ר\rb*\rb |לְמִנְיָ֖ן\rb* \rb male goats|וּצְפִירֵ֨י\rb*\rb |עִזִּ֜ין\rb*, \rb one for each tribe|שִׁבְטֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb They also appointed|וַהֲקִ֨ימוּ\rb* \rb the priests|כָהֲנַיָּ֜א\rb* \rb by their divisions|בִּפְלֻגָּתְה֗וֹן\rb* \rb and the Levites|וְלֵוָיֵא֙\rb* \rb by their groups|בְּמַחְלְקָ֣תְה֔וֹן\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the service|עֲבִידַ֥ת\rb* \rb of God|אֱלָהָ֖א\rb*\rb |דִּ֣י\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִירוּשְׁלֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb according to what is written|כִּכְתָ֖ב\rb* \rb in the Book|סְפַ֥ר\rb* \rb of Moses|מֹשֶֽׁה׃פ\rb*.
\s1 The Returned Exiles Keep the Passover
\p \v 19 \rb On the fourteenth day|בְּאַרְבָּעָ֥ה\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֖ר\rb* \rb of the first|הָרִאשֽׁוֹן׃\rb* \rb month|לַחֹ֥דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb the exiles|בְנֵי־\rb*\rb |הַגּוֹלָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb kept|וַיַּעֲשׂ֥וּ\rb* \rb the Passover|הַפָּ֑סַח\rb*. \v 20 \rb All|כֻּלָּ֣ם\rb* \rb the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֧ים\rb* \rb and Levites|וְהַלְוִיִּ֛ם\rb*\rb |כְּאֶחָ֖ד\rb*\rb |כִּ֣י\rb* \rb had purified themselves|הִֽטַּהֲר֞וּ\rb* \rb and were ceremonially clean|טְהוֹרִ֑ים\rb*.
\p \rb And the Levites slaughtered|וַיִּשְׁחֲט֤וּ\rb* \rb the Passover lamb|הַפֶּ֙סַח֙\rb* \rb for all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the exiles|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |הַגּוֹלָ֔ה\rb*, \rb for their priestly|הַכֹּהֲנִ֖ים\rb* \rb brothers|וְלַאֲחֵיהֶ֥ם\rb*, \rb and for themselves|וְלָהֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 21 \rb The Israelites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb who had returned|הַשָּׁבִים֙\rb* \rb from exile|מֵֽהַגּוֹלָ֔ה\rb* \rb ate it|וַיֹּאכְל֣וּ\rb*, \rb together with all|וְכֹ֗ל\rb* \rb who had separated themselves|הַנִּבְדָּ֛ל\rb* \rb from the uncleanness|מִטֻּמְאַ֥ת\rb* \rb of the peoples|גּוֹיֵֽ־\rb*\f + \fr 6:21 \ft Or \fqa nations\f* \rb of the land|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb*\rb |אֲלֵהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb to seek|לִדְרֹ֕שׁ\rb* \rb the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*.
\p \v 22 \rb For seven|שִׁבְעַ֥ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֖ים\rb* \rb they kept|וַיַּֽעֲשׂ֧וּ\rb* \rb the Feast|חַג־\rb* \rb of Unleavened Bread|מַצּ֛וֹת\rb*\f + \fr 6:22 \ft That is, the seven-day period after the Passover during which no leaven may be eaten; see Exodus 12:14–20.\f* \rb with joy|בְּשִׂמְחָ֑ה\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֣י׀\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb had made them joyful|שִׂמְּחָ֣ם\rb* \rb and turned|וְֽהֵסֵ֞ב\rb* \rb the heart|לֵ֤ב\rb* \rb of the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Assyria|אַשּׁוּר֙\rb* \rb toward them|עֲלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb to strengthen|לְחַזֵּ֣ק\rb* \rb their hands|יְדֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb in the work|בִּמְלֶ֥אכֶת\rb* \rb on the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of the God|הָאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃פ\rb*.
\c 7
\s1 Ezra Arrives in Jerusalem
\p \v 1 \rb Many years later|וְאַחַר֙\rb*\rb |הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb*\rb |הַדְּבָרִ֣ים\rb*,\f + \fr 7:1 \ft Literally \fqa After these things\f* \rb during the reign|בְּמַלְכ֖וּת\rb* \rb of Artaxerxes|אַרְתַּחְשַׁ֣סְתְּא\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Persia|פָּרָ֑ס\rb*, \rb Ezra|עֶזְרָא֙\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Seraiah|שְׂרָיָ֔ה\rb*, \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Azariah|עֲזַרְיָ֖ה\rb*, \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Hilkiah|חִלְקִיָּֽה׃\rb*, \v 2 \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Shallum|שַׁלּ֥וּם\rb*, \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Zadok|צָד֖וֹק\rb*, \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Ahitub|אֲחִיטֽוּב׃\rb*, \v 3 \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Amariah|אֲמַרְיָ֥ה\rb*, \rb the son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Azariah|עֲזַרְיָ֖ה\rb*, \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Meraioth|מְרָיֽוֹת׃\rb*, \v 4 \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Zerahiah|זְרַֽחְיָ֥ה\rb*, \rb the son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Uzzi|עֻזִּ֖י\rb*, \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Bukki|בֻּקִּֽי׃\rb*, \v 5 \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Abishua|אֲבִישׁ֗וּעַ\rb*, \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Phinehas|פִּֽינְחָס֙\rb*, \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Eleazar|אֶלְעָזָ֔ר\rb*, \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֥ן\rb* \rb the chief|הָרֹֽאשׁ׃\rb* \rb priest|הַכֹּהֵ֖ן\rb*— \v 6 \rb this|ה֤וּא\rb* \rb Ezra|עֶזְרָא֙\rb* \rb came up|עָלָ֣ה\rb* \rb from Babylon|מִבָּבֶ֔ל\rb*. \rb He was|וְהֽוּא־\rb* \rb a scribe|סֹפֵ֤ר\rb* \rb skilled|מָהִיר֙\rb* \rb in the Law|בְּתוֹרַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb*, \rb which|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb had given|נָתַ֥ן\rb*.
\p \rb The king|הַמֶּ֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb had granted|וַיִּתֶּן־\rb* \rb Ezra|ל֣וֹ\rb* \rb all|כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb his requests|בַּקָּשָׁתֽוֹ׃פ\rb*, \rb for the hand|כְּיַד־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb his God|אֱלֹהָיו֙\rb* \rb was upon him|עָלָ֔יו\rb*. \v 7 \rb So in the seventh|שֶׁ֖בַע\rb* \rb year|בִּשְׁנַת־\rb* \rb of King|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb* \rb Artaxerxes|לְאַרְתַּחְשַׁ֥סְתְּא\rb*, \rb he went up|וַיַּֽעֲל֣וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb with some of|וּמִן־\rb* \rb the Israelites|מִבְּנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִ֠שְׂרָאֵל\rb*, \rb including priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֨ים\rb*, \rb Levites|וְהַלְוִיִּ֜ם\rb*, \rb singers|וְהַמְשֹׁרְרִ֧ים\rb*, \rb gatekeepers|וְהַשֹּׁעֲרִ֛ים\rb*, \rb and temple servants|וְהַנְּתִינִ֖ים\rb*.\f + \fr 7:7 \ft Hebrew \fqa Nethinim\ft ; also in verse 24\f*
\p \v 8 \rb Ezra arrived|וַיָּבֹ֥א\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb* \rb in the fifth|הַחֲמִישִׁ֑י\rb*\rb |הִ֛יא\rb* \rb month|בַּחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִ֖ית\rb* \rb year|שְׁנַ֥ת\rb* \rb of the king|לַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb |כִּ֗י\rb* \rb He|ה֣וּא\rb* \rb had begun|יְסֻ֔ד\rb* \rb the journey|הַֽמַּעֲלָ֖ה\rb* \rb from Babylon|מִבָּבֶ֑ל\rb* \rb on the first day|בְּאֶחָד֙\rb* \rb of the first|הָרִאשׁ֔וֹן\rb* \rb month|לַחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb and he arrived|בָּ֚א\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb on the first|וּבְאֶחָ֞ד\rb* \rb day of the fifth|הַחֲמִישִׁ֗י\rb* \rb month|לַחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb for the gracious|הַטּוֹבָ֥ה\rb* \rb hand|כְּיַד־\rb* \rb of his God|אֱלֹהָ֖יו\rb* \rb was upon him|עָלָֽיו׃\rb*. \v 10 \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb Ezra|עֶזְרָא֙\rb* \rb had set|הֵכִ֣ין\rb* \rb his heart|לְבָב֔וֹ\rb* \rb to study|לִדְר֛וֹשׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Law|תּוֹרַ֥ת\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb to practice it|וְלַעֲשֹׂ֑ת\rb*, \rb and to teach|וּלְלַמֵּ֥ד\rb* \rb its statutes|חֹ֥ק\rb* \rb and ordinances|וּמִשְׁפָּֽט׃ס\rb* \rb in Israel|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*.
\s1 Artaxerxes’ Letter for Ezra
\p \v 11 \rb This|וְזֶ֣ה׀\rb* \rb is the text|פַּרְשֶׁ֣גֶן\rb* \rb of the letter|הַֽנִּשְׁתְּוָ֗ן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Artaxerxes|אַרְתַּחְשַׁ֔סְתְּא\rb* \rb had given|נָתַן֙\rb* \rb to Ezra|לְעֶזְרָ֥א\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֖ן\rb* \rb and scribe|הַסֹּפֵ֑ר\rb*, \rb an expert|סֹפֵ֞ר\rb*\rb |דִּבְרֵ֧י\rb* \rb in the commandments|מִצְוֺת־\rb* \rb and statutes|וְחֻקָּ֖יו\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃פ\rb*:\f + \fr 7:11 \ft The original text of Ezra 7:12–26 is in Aramaic.\f*
\p \v 12 \rb Artaxerxes|אַ֨רְתַּחְשַׁ֔סְתְּא\rb*, \rb king|מֶ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb of kings|מַלְכַיָּ֑א\rb*.
\p \rb To Ezra|לְעֶזְרָ֣א\rb* \rb the priest|כָ֠הֲנָא\rb*, \rb the scribe|סָפַ֨ר\rb* \rb of the Law|דָּתָ֜א\rb* \rb of|דִּֽי־\rb* \rb the God|אֱלָ֧הּ\rb* \rb of heaven|שְׁמַיָּ֛א\rb*:
\p \rb Greetings|גְּמִ֖יר\rb*\rb |וּכְעֶֽנֶת׃\rb*.\f + \fr 7:12 \ft Aramaic \fqa Perfect now \ft (probably a greeting)\f*
\p \v 13 \rb I|מִנִּי֮\rb* \rb hereby|שִׂ֣ים\rb* \rb decree|טְעֵם֒\rb* \rb that|דִּ֣י\rb* \rb any|כָל־\rb* \rb volunteers|מִתְנַדַּ֣ב\rb* \rb among the Israelites|עַמָּ֨ה\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֜ל\rb* \rb in my kingdom|בְּמַלְכוּתִי֩\rb*,\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb including the priests|וְכָהֲנ֣וֹהִי\rb* \rb and Levites|וְלֵוָיֵ֗א\rb*, \rb may go up|יְהָֽךְ׃\rb* \rb with you|עִמָּ֖ךְ\rb*\rb |לִמְהָ֧ךְ\rb* \rb to Jerusalem|לִֽירוּשְׁלֶ֛ם\rb*. \v 14 \rb |כָּל־\rb*\rb |קֳבֵ֗ל\rb* \rb You are sent|שְׁלִ֔יחַ\rb* \rb by|מִן־\rb*\rb |קֳדָ֨ם\rb* \rb the king|מַלְכָּ֜א\rb* \rb and his seven|וְשִׁבְעַ֤ת\rb* \rb counselors|יָעֲטֹ֙הִי֙\rb* \rb to evaluate|לְבַקָּרָ֥א\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb Judah|יְה֖וּד\rb* \rb and Jerusalem|וְלִֽירוּשְׁלֶ֑ם\rb* \rb according to the Law|בְּדָ֥ת\rb* \rb of your God|אֱלָהָ֖ךְ\rb*, \rb which|דִּ֥י\rb* \rb is in your hand|בִידָֽךְ׃\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb Moreover, you are to take with you|וּלְהֵיבָלָ֖ה\rb* \rb the silver|כְּסַ֣ף\rb* \rb and gold|וּדְהַ֑ב\rb* \rb that|דִּֽי־\rb* \rb the king|מַלְכָּ֣א\rb* \rb and his counselors|וְיָעֲט֗וֹהִי\rb* \rb have freely offered|הִתְנַדַּ֙בוּ֙\rb* \rb to the God|לֶאֱלָ֣הּ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb whose|דִּ֥י\rb* \rb dwelling|מִשְׁכְּנֵֽהּ׃\rb* \rb is in Jerusalem|בִֽירוּשְׁלֶ֖ם\rb*, \v 16 \rb together with all|וְכֹל֙\rb* \rb the silver|כְּסַ֣ף\rb* \rb and gold|וּדְהַ֔ב\rb*\rb |דִּ֣י\rb* \rb you may find|תְהַשְׁכַּ֔ח\rb* \rb in all|בְּכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb the province|מְדִינַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֑ל\rb*, \rb as well as|עִם֩\rb* \rb the freewill offerings|הִתְנַדָּב֨וּת\rb* \rb of the people|עַמָּ֤א\rb* \rb and priests|וְכָֽהֲנַיָּא֙\rb*\rb |מִֽתְנַדְּבִ֔ין\rb* \rb to the house|לְבֵ֥ית\rb* \rb of their God|אֱלָהֲהֹ֖ם\rb*\rb |דִּ֥י\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִירוּשְׁלֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 17 \rb With this|דְנָ֗ה\rb* \rb money|בְּכַסְפָּ֣א\rb*,\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb therefore|דְּנָה֩\rb*, \rb you are to buy|תִקְנֵ֜א\rb* \rb as many bulls|תּוֹרִ֤ין׀\rb*, \rb rams|דִּכְרִין֙\rb*, \rb and lambs|אִמְּרִ֔ין\rb* \rb as needed|אָסְפַּ֨רְנָא\rb*, \rb together with their grain offerings|וּמִנְחָתְה֖וֹן\rb* \rb and drink offerings|וְנִסְכֵּיה֑וֹן\rb*, \rb and offer|וּתְקָרֵ֣ב\rb* \rb them|הִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb on|עַֽל־\rb* \rb the altar|מַדְבְּחָ֔ה\rb*\rb |דִּ֛י\rb* \rb at the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of your God|אֱלָהֲכֹ֖ם\rb*\rb |דִּ֥י\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִירוּשְׁלֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 18 \rb You and your brothers|אֶחַיִךְ\rb* \rb may do|לְמֶעְבַּ֑ד\rb* \rb whatever|וּמָ֣ה\rb*\rb |דִי֩\rb*\rb |עֲלַיִךְ\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb seems best|יֵיטַ֗ב\rb* \rb with the rest|בִּשְׁאָ֛ר\rb* \rb of the silver|כַּסְפָּ֥א\rb* \rb and gold|וְדַהֲבָ֖ה\rb*, \rb according to the will|כִּרְע֥וּת\rb* \rb of your God|אֱלָהֲכֹ֖ם\rb*\rb |תַּעַבְדֽוּן׃\rb*.
\p \v 19 \rb You must deliver|הַשְׁלֵ֕ם\rb* \rb to|קֳדָ֖ם\rb* \rb the God|אֱלָהָ֑ךְ\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְרוּשְׁלֶֽם׃\rb* \rb all the articles|וּמָֽאנַיָּא֙\rb*\rb |דִּֽי־\rb* \rb given|מִתְיַהֲבִ֣ין\rb* \rb to you|לָ֔ךְ\rb* \rb for the service|לְפָלְחָ֖ן\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of your God|אֱלָ֥הּ\rb*. \v 20 \rb And if anything else|וּשְׁאָ֗ר\rb* \rb is needed|חַשְׁחוּת֙\rb* \rb for the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of your God|אֱלָהָ֔ךְ\rb* \rb that|דִּ֥י\rb* \rb you|לָ֖ךְ\rb* \rb may have occasion|יִפֶּל־\rb* \rb to supply|לְמִנְתַּ֑ן\rb*, \rb you may pay for it|תִּנְתֵּ֕ן\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the royal|מַלְכָּֽא׃\rb*\rb |בֵּ֖ית\rb* \rb treasury|גִּנְזֵ֥י\rb*.
\p \v 21 \rb |וּ֠מִנִּי\rb* \rb I|אֲנָ֞ה\rb*, \rb King|מַלְכָּא֙\rb* \rb Artaxerxes|אַרְתַּחְשַׁ֤סְתְּא\rb*,\rb |שִׂ֣ים\rb* \rb decree|טְעֵ֔ם\rb* \rb to all|לְכֹל֙\rb* \rb the treasurers|גִּזַּֽבְרַיָּ֔א\rb*\rb |דִּ֖י\rb* \rb west|בַּעֲבַ֣ר\rb* \rb of the Euphrates|נַהֲרָ֑ה\rb*:\f + \fr 7:21 \ft Aramaic \fqa beyond the River\ft ; also in verse 25\f* \rb Whatever|כָל־\rb*\rb |דִּ֣י\rb* \rb Ezra|עֶזְרָ֨א\rb* \rb the priest|כָהֲנָ֜ה\rb*, \rb the scribe|סָפַ֤ר\rb* \rb of the Law|דָּתָא֙\rb* \rb of the God|אֱלָ֣הּ\rb* \rb of heaven|שְׁמַיָּ֔א\rb*, \rb may require of you|יִ֠שְׁאֲלֶנְכוֹן\rb*, \rb it must be provided|יִתְעֲבִֽד׃\rb* \rb promptly|אָסְפַּ֖רְנָא\rb*, \v 22 \rb up to|עַד־\rb* \rb a hundred|מְאָה֒\rb* \rb talents|כַּכְּרִ֣ין\rb*\rb |וְעַד־\rb* \rb of silver|כְּסַף֮\rb*,\f + \fr 7:22 \fqa 100 talents \ft is approximately 3.77 tons or 3.42 metric tons of silver.\f* \rb a hundred|מְאָ֔ה\rb* \rb cors|כֹּרִ֣ין\rb* \rb of wheat|חִנְטִין֙\rb*,\f + \fr 7:22 \fqa 100 cors \ft is approximately 624 bushels or 22,000 liters (probably about 19.2 tons or 17.4 metric tons of wheat).\f*\rb |וְעַד־\rb* \rb a hundred|מְאָ֔ה\rb* \rb baths|בַּתִּ֣ין\rb*\rb |וְעַד־\rb* \rb of wine|חֲמַר֙\rb*,\f + \fr 7:22 \fqa 100 baths \ft is approximately 580 gallons or 2,200 liters of wine.\f* \rb a hundred|מְאָ֑ה\rb* \rb baths|בַּתִּ֥ין\rb* \rb of olive oil|מְשַׁ֖ח\rb*,\f + \fr 7:22 \ft Or \fqa 100 baths of oil\ft ; that is, approximately 580 gallons or 2,200 liters\f* \rb and salt|וּמְלַ֖ח\rb*\rb |דִּי־\rb* \rb without|לָ֥א\rb* \rb limit|כְתָֽב׃\rb*. \v 23 \rb Whatever|כָּל־\rb*\rb |דִּ֗י\rb* \rb is commanded|טַ֙עַם֙\rb* \rb by|מִן־\rb* \rb the God|אֱלָ֣הּ\rb* \rb of heaven|שְׁמַיָּ֔א\rb* \rb must be done|יִתְעֲבֵד֙\rb* \rb diligently|אַדְרַזְדָּ֔א\rb* \rb for His house|לְבֵ֖ית\rb*\rb |אֱלָ֣הּ\rb*\rb |שְׁמַיָּ֑א\rb*. \rb For|דִּֽי־\rb* \rb why|לְמָ֤ה\rb* \rb should wrath|קְצַ֔ף\rb* \rb fall|לֶֽהֱוֵא֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the realm|מַלְכ֥וּת\rb* \rb of the king|מַלְכָּ֖א\rb* \rb and his sons|וּבְנֽוֹהִי׃\rb*? \v 24 \rb And|וּלְכֹ֣ם\rb* \rb be advised|מְהוֹדְעִ֗ין\rb* \rb that|דִּ֣י\rb* \rb you have no|לָ֥א\rb* \rb authority|שַׁלִּ֖יט\rb* \rb to impose|לְמִרְמֵ֥א\rb* \rb tribute|מִנְדָּ֤ה\rb*, \rb duty|בְלוֹ֙\rb*, \rb or toll|וַהֲלָ֔ךְ\rb* \rb on|עֲלֵיהֹֽם׃\rb* \rb any|כָל־\rb* \rb of the priests|כָּהֲנַיָּ֣א\rb*, \rb Levites|וְ֠לֵוָיֵא\rb*, \rb singers|זַמָּ֨רַיָּ֤א\rb*, \rb doorkeepers|תָרָֽעַיָּא֙\rb*, \rb temple servants|נְתִ֣ינַיָּ֔א\rb*, \rb or other servants|וּפָ֣לְחֵ֔י\rb* \rb of this|דְנָ֑ה\rb* \rb house|בֵּ֖ית\rb* \rb of God|אֱלָהָ֣א\rb*.
\p \v 25 \rb And you|וְאַ֣נְתְּ\rb*, \rb Ezra|עֶזְרָ֗א\rb*, \rb according to the wisdom|כְּחָכְמַ֨ת\rb* \rb of your God|אֱלָהָ֤ךְ\rb*, \rb which you possess|דִּֽי־\rb*\rb |בִידָךְ֙\rb*, \rb are to appoint|מֶ֣נִּי\rb* \rb magistrates|שָׁפְטִ֞ין\rb* \rb and judges|וְדַיָּנִ֗ין\rb* \rb to judge|דָּאֲנִין\rb* \rb all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the people|עַמָּה֙\rb*\rb |דִּ֚י\rb* \rb west|בַּעֲבַ֣ר\rb* \rb of the Euphrates|נַהֲרָ֔ה\rb* — \rb all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb who know|יָדְעֵ֖י\rb* \rb the laws|דָּתֵ֣י\rb* \rb of your God|אֱלָהָ֑ךְ\rb*. \rb And you are to teach these laws|יָדַ֖ע\rb* \rb to anyone who|וְדִ֧י\rb* \rb does not|לָ֦א\rb* \rb know them|תְּהוֹדְעֽוּן׃\rb*. \v 26 \rb If anyone|וְכָל־\rb*\rb |דִּי־\rb* \rb does|לֶהֱוֵ֨א\rb* \rb not|לָא֩\rb* \rb keep|עָבֵ֜ד\rb* \rb the law|דָּתָ֣א\rb* \rb of|דִֽי־\rb* \rb your God|אֱלָהָ֗ךְ\rb* \rb and the law|וְדָתָא֙\rb* \rb of|דִּ֣י\rb* \rb the king|מַלְכָּ֔א\rb*, \rb let a strict|אָסְפַּ֕רְנָא\rb* \rb judgment|דִּינָ֕ה\rb* \rb be|לֶהֱוֵ֥א\rb* \rb executed|מִתְעֲבֵ֖ד\rb* \rb against him|מִנֵּ֑הּ\rb*, \rb whether|הֵ֤ן\rb* \rb death|לְמוֹת֙\rb*,\rb |הֵ֣ן\rb* \rb banishment|לִשְׁרֹשׁוּ\rb*,\rb |הֵן־\rb* \rb confiscation|לַעֲנָ֥שׁ\rb* \rb of property|נִכְסִ֖ין\rb*, \rb or imprisonment|וְלֶאֱסוּרִֽין׃פ\rb*.
\s1 Ezra Blesses God
\p \v 27 \rb Blessed be|בָּר֥וּךְ\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of our fathers|אֲבוֹתֵ֑ינוּ\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb has put|נָתַ֤ן\rb*\rb |כָּזֹאת֙\rb* \rb into the heart|בְּלֵ֣ב\rb* \rb of the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb to so honor|לְפָאֵ֕ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb*, \v 28 \rb and who has shown|הִטָּה־\rb* \rb me|וְעָלַ֣י\rb* \rb favor|חֶ֗סֶד\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֤י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb*, \rb his counselors|וְיֽוֹעֲצָ֔יו\rb*, \rb and all|וּלְכָל־\rb* \rb his|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb powerful|הַגִּבֹּרִ֑ים\rb* \rb officials|שָׂרֵ֥י\rb*.
\p \rb And because the hand|כְּיַד־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb my God|אֱלֹהַי֙\rb* \rb was upon me|עָלַ֔י\rb*, \rb I|וַאֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb took courage|הִתְחַזַּ֗קְתִּי\rb* \rb and gathered|וָאֶקְבְּצָ֧ה\rb* \rb the leaders|רָאשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb of Israel|מִיִּשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb to return|לַעֲל֥וֹת\rb* \rb with me|עִמִּֽי׃פ\rb*.
\c 8
\s1 The Exiles Who Returned with Ezra
\p \v 1 \rb These|וְאֵ֛לֶּה\rb* \rb are the family|אֲבֹתֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb heads|רָאשֵׁ֥י\rb* \rb and genealogical records|וְהִתְיַחְשָׂ֑ם\rb* \rb of those who returned|הָעֹלִ֣ים\rb* \rb with me|עִמִּ֗י\rb* \rb from Babylon|מִבָּבֶֽל׃ס\rb* \rb during the reign|בְּמַלְכ֛וּת\rb* \rb of King|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb Artaxerxes|אַרְתַּחְשַׁ֥סְתְּא\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \v 2 \rb from the descendants|מִבְּנֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Phinehas|פִֽינְחָס֙\rb*, \rb Gershom|גֵּֽרְשֹׁ֔םס\rb*;
\li1 \rb from the descendants|מִבְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Ithamar|אִיתָמָ֖ר\rb*, \rb Daniel|דָּנִיֵּ֑אלס\rb*;
\li1 \rb from the descendants of|מִבְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb David|דָוִ֖יד\rb*, \rb Hattush|חַטּֽוּשׁ׃ס\rb* \v 3 \rb of the descendants|מִבְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Shecaniah|שְׁכַנְיָ֔הס\rb*;
\li1 \rb from the descendants|מִבְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Parosh|פַרְעֹ֖שׁ\rb*, \rb Zechariah|זְכַרְיָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and with him|וְעִמּ֛וֹ\rb* \rb were registered|הִתְיַחֵ֥שׂ\rb* \rb 150|מֵאָ֥ה\rb*\rb |וַחֲמִשִּֽׁים׃ס\rb* \rb men|לִזְכָרִ֖ים\rb*;
\li1 \v 4 \rb from the descendants|מִבְּנֵי֙\rb*\rb |פַּחַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Pahath-Moab|מוֹאָ֔ב\rb*, \rb Eliehoenai|אֶלְיְהֽוֹעֵינַ֖י\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Zerahiah|זְרַֽחְיָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and with him|וְעִמּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb 200|מָאתַ֥יִם\rb* \rb men|הַזְּכָרִֽים׃ס\rb*;
\li1 \v 5 \rb from the descendants of Zattu|מִבְּנֵ֥י\rb*, \rb Shecaniah|שְׁכַנְיָ֖ה\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jahaziel|יַחֲזִיאֵ֑ל\rb*,\f + \fr 8:5 \ft Some LXX manuscripts (see also 1 Esdras 8:32); Hebrew \fqa from the descendants of Shecaniah, the son of Jahaziel\f* \rb and with him|וְעִמּ֕וֹ\rb* \rb 300|שְׁלֹ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |מֵא֖וֹת\rb* \rb men|הַזְּכָרִֽים׃ס\rb*;
\li1 \v 6 \rb from the descendants|וּמִבְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Adin|עָדִ֔ין\rb*, \rb Ebed|עֶ֖בֶד\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jonathan|יוֹנָתָ֑ן\rb*, \rb and with him|וְעִמּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb 50|חֲמִשִּׁ֥ים\rb* \rb men|הַזְּכָרִֽים׃ס\rb*;
\li1 \v 7 \rb from the descendants|וּמִבְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Elam|עֵילָ֔ם\rb*, \rb Jeshaiah|יְשַֽׁעְיָ֖ה\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Athaliah|עֲתַלְיָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and with him|וְעִמּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb 70|שִׁבְעִ֥ים\rb* \rb men|הַזְּכָרִֽים׃ס\rb*;
\li1 \v 8 \rb from the descendants|וּמִבְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Shephatiah|שְׁפַטְיָ֔ה\rb*, \rb Zebadiah|זְבַדְיָ֖ה\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Michael|מִֽיכָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb and with him|וְעִמּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb 80|שְׁמֹנִ֥ים\rb* \rb men|הַזְּכָרִֽים׃ס\rb*;
\li1 \v 9 \rb from the descendants|מִבְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Joab|יוֹאָ֔ב\rb*, \rb Obadiah|עֹבַדְיָ֖ה\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jehiel|יְחִיאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb and with him|וְעִמּ֕וֹ\rb* \rb 218|מָאתַ֛יִם\rb*\rb |וּשְׁמֹנָ֥ה\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֖ר\rb* \rb men|הַזְּכָרִֽים׃ס\rb*;
\li1 \v 10 \rb from the descendants of Bani|וּמִבְּנֵ֥י\rb*, \rb Shelomith|שְׁלוֹמִ֖ית\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Josiphiah|יוֹסִפְיָ֑ה\rb*,\f + \fr 8:10 \ft Some LXX manuscripts (see also 1 Esdras 8:36); Hebrew \fqa from the descendants of Shelomith, the son of Josiphiah\f* \rb and with him|וְעִמּ֕וֹ\rb* \rb 160|מֵאָ֥ה\rb*\rb |וְשִׁשִּׁ֖ים\rb* \rb men|הַזְּכָרִֽים׃ס\rb*;
\li1 \v 11 \rb from the descendants|וּמִבְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Bebai|בֵבַ֔י\rb*, \rb Zechariah|זְכַרְיָ֖ה\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Bebai|בֵּבָ֑י\rb*, \rb and with him|וְעִמּ֕וֹ\rb* \rb 28|עֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb*\rb |וּשְׁמֹנָ֖ה\rb* \rb men|הַזְּכָרִֽים׃ס\rb*;
\li1 \v 12 \rb from the descendants|וּמִבְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Azgad|עַזְגָּ֔ד\rb*, \rb Johanan|יוֹחָנָ֖ן\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Hakkatan|הַקָּטָ֑ן\rb*, \rb and with him|וְעִמּ֕וֹ\rb* \rb 110|מֵאָ֥ה\rb*\rb |וַעֲשָׂרָ֖ה\rb* \rb men|הַזְּכָרִֽים׃ס\rb*;
\li1 \v 13 \rb from the later|אַחֲרֹנִים֒\rb*\f + \fr 8:13 \ft Or \fqa the last\f* \rb descendants|וּמִבְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Adonikam|אֲדֹנִיקָם֮\rb*, \rb these|וְאֵ֣לֶּה\rb* \rb were their names|שְׁמוֹתָ֔ם\rb*: \rb Eliphelet|אֱלִיפֶ֖לֶט\rb*, \rb Jeiel|יְעִיאֵ֣ל\rb*, \rb and Shemaiah|וּֽשְׁמַעְיָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and with them|וְעִמָּהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb 60|שִׁשִּׁ֥ים\rb* \rb men|הַזְּכָרִֽים׃ס\rb*;
\li1 \v 14 \rb and from the descendants|וּמִבְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Bigvai|בִגְוַ֖י\rb*, \rb both Uthai|עוּתַ֣י\rb* \rb and Zaccur|וְזָבוּד\rb*,\f + \fr 8:14 \ft LXX, Syriac, and an alternate MT reading; the other alternate reads \fqa Zabbud\ft .\f* \rb and with them|וְעִמּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb 70|שִׁבְעִ֥ים\rb* \rb men|הַזְּכָרִֽים׃פ\rb*.
\s1 Ezra Sends for the Levites
\p \v 15 \rb Now I assembled these exiles|וָֽאֶקְבְּצֵ֗ם\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb the canal|הַנָּהָר֙\rb* \rb that flows|הַבָּ֣א\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Ahava|אַהֲוָ֔א\rb*, \rb and we camped|וַנַּחֲנֶ֥ה\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb three|שְׁלֹשָׁ֑ה\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֣ים\rb*. \rb And when I searched|וָאָבִ֤ינָה\rb* \rb among the people|בָעָם֙\rb* \rb and priests|וּבַכֹּ֣הֲנִ֔ים\rb*, \rb I found|מָצָ֥אתִי\rb* \rb no|לֹא־\rb* \rb Levites|וּמִבְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |לֵוִ֖י\rb* \rb there|שָֽׁם׃\rb*.
\p \v 16 \rb Then I summoned|וָאֶשְׁלְחָ֡ה\rb* \rb the leaders|רָאשִׁ֑ים\rb*: \rb Eliezer|לֶאֱלִיעֶ֡זֶר\rb*, \rb Ariel|לַאֲרִיאֵ֡ל\rb*, \rb Shemaiah|לִֽ֠שְׁמַעְיָה\rb*, \rb Elnathan|וּלְאֶלְנָתָ֨ן\rb*,\f + \fr 8:16 \fqa Elnathan \ft appears three times in verse, either as a repetition for emphasis or as a record of multiple men with this name.\f* \rb Jarib|וּלְיָרִ֜יב\rb*, \rb Elnathan|וּלְאֶלְנָתָ֧ן\rb*, \rb Nathan|וּלְנָתָ֛ן\rb*, \rb Zechariah|וְלִזְכַרְיָ֥ה\rb*, \rb and Meshullam|וְלִמְשֻׁלָּ֖ם\rb*, \rb as well as the teachers|מְבִינִֽים׃\rb* \rb Joiarib|וּלְיוֹיָרִ֥יב\rb* \rb and Elnathan|וּלְאֶלְנָתָ֖ן\rb*. \v 17 \rb And I sent|וָאוֹצִאָה\rb* \rb them|אוֹתָם֙\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb Iddo|אִדּ֣וֹ\rb*, \rb the leader|הָרֹ֔אשׁ\rb* \rb at Casiphia|בְּכָסִפְיָ֖א\rb*,\rb |הַמָּק֑וֹם\rb*\rb |וָאָשִׂימָה֩\rb*\rb |בְּפִיהֶ֨ם\rb* \rb with a message|דְּבָרִ֜ים\rb*\rb |לְ֠דַבֵּר\rb* \rb for|אֶל־\rb* \rb him|אִדּ֨וֹ\rb* \rb and his kinsmen|אָחִ֤יו\rb*, \rb the temple servants|הַנְּתוּנִים\rb*\f + \fr 8:17 \ft Hebrew \fqa the Nethinim\ft ; also in verse 20\f* \rb at Casiphia|בְּכָסִפְיָ֣א\rb*,\rb |הַמָּק֔וֹם\rb* \rb that they should bring|לְהָֽבִיא־\rb* \rb to us|לָ֥נוּ\rb* \rb ministers|מְשָׁרְתִ֖ים\rb* \rb for the house|לְבֵ֥ית\rb* \rb of our God|אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb And since the gracious|הַטּוֹבָ֤ה\rb* \rb hand|כְּיַד־\rb* \rb of our God|אֱלֹהֵ֨ינוּ\rb* \rb was upon us|עָלֵ֙ינוּ֙\rb*, \rb they brought|וַיָּבִ֨יאּוּ\rb* \rb us|לָ֜נוּ\rb* \rb Sherebiah|וְשֵׁרֵֽבְיָ֛ה\rb*— \rb a man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of insight|שֶׂ֔כֶל\rb* \rb from the descendants|מִבְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Mahli|מַחְלִ֔י\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Levi|לֵוִ֖י\rb*, \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*— \rb along with his sons|וּבָנָ֥יו\rb* \rb and brothers|וְאֶחָ֖יו\rb*, \rb 18|שְׁמֹנָ֥ה\rb* \rb men|עָשָֽׂר׃\rb*; \v 19 \rb also|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Hashabiah|חֲשַׁבְיָ֔ה\rb*, \rb together with|וְאִתּ֥וֹ\rb* \rb Jeshaiah|יְשַֽׁעְיָ֖ה\rb*, \rb from the descendants|מִבְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Merari|מְרָרִ֑י\rb*, \rb and his brothers|אֶחָ֥יו\rb* \rb and their sons|וּבְנֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*, \rb 20 men|עֶשְׂרִֽים׃ס\rb*. \v 20 \rb They also brought 220|מָאתַ֣יִם\rb*\rb |וְעֶשְׂרִ֑ים\rb* \rb of|וּמִן־\rb* \rb the temple servants|הַנְּתִינִ֗ים\rb*, \rb all|כֻּלָּ֖ם\rb* \rb designated|נִקְּב֥וּ\rb* \rb by name|בְשֵׁמֽוֹת׃\rb*. \rb David|דָּוִ֤יד\rb* \rb and the officials|וְהַשָּׂרִים֙\rb* \rb had appointed|שֶׁנָּתַ֨ן\rb* \rb them|נְתִינִ֖ים\rb* \rb to assist|לַעֲבֹדַ֣ת\rb* \rb the Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֔ם\rb*.
\s1 Fasting for Protection
\p \v 21 \rb And there by|עַל־\rb* \rb the Ahava|אַהֲוָ֔א\rb* \rb Canal|הַנָּהָ֣ר\rb* \rb I proclaimed|וָאֶקְרָ֨א\rb*\rb |שָׁ֥ם\rb* \rb a fast|צוֹם֙\rb*, \rb so that we might humble|לְהִתְעַנּ֖וֹת\rb* \rb ourselves before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵ֑ינוּ\rb* \rb and ask Him for|לְבַקֵּ֤שׁ\rb*\rb |מִמֶּ֙נּוּ֙\rb* \rb a safe|יְשָׁרָ֔ה\rb* \rb journey|דֶּ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb for us|לָ֥נוּ\rb* \rb and our children|וּלְטַפֵּ֖נוּ\rb*, \rb with all|וּלְכָל־\rb* \rb our possessions|רְכוּשֵֽׁנוּ׃\rb*. \v 22 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb I was ashamed|בֹ֗שְׁתִּי\rb* \rb to ask the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb for|לִשְׁא֤וֹל\rb* \rb an escort of soldiers|חַ֣יִל\rb* \rb and horsemen|וּפָרָשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb to protect us|לְעָזְרֵ֥נוּ\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb our enemies|מֵאוֹיֵ֖ב\rb* \rb on the road|בַּדָּ֑רֶךְ\rb*, \rb since|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb we had told him|אָמַ֨רְנוּ\rb*\rb |לַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb*, “\rb The hand|יַד־\rb* \rb of our God|אֱלֹהֵ֤ינוּ\rb* \rb is gracious|לְטוֹבָ֔ה\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb who seek Him|מְבַקְשָׁיו֙\rb*, \rb but His great|וְעֻזּ֣וֹ\rb* \rb anger|וְאַפּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb is against|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb who forsake Him|עֹזְבָֽיו׃\rb*.”
\p \v 23 \rb So we fasted|וַנָּצ֛וּמָה\rb* \rb and petitioned|וַנְּבַקְשָׁ֥ה\rb* \rb our God|מֵאֱלֹהֵ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb about|עַל־\rb* \rb this|זֹ֑את\rb*, \rb and He granted our request|וַיֵּעָתֵ֖ר\rb*.
\s1 Priests to Guard the Offerings
\p \v 24 \rb Then I set apart|וָאַבְדִּ֛ילָה\rb* \rb twelve|שְׁנֵ֣ים\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֑ר\rb* \rb of the leading|מִשָּׂרֵ֥י\rb* \rb priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֖ים\rb*, \rb together with Sherebiah|לְשֵׁרֵֽבְיָ֣ה\rb*, \rb Hashabiah|חֲשַׁבְיָ֔ה\rb*, \rb and|וְעִמָּהֶ֥ם\rb* \rb ten|עֲשָׂרָֽה׃\rb* \rb of their brothers|מֵאֲחֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*, \v 25 \rb and I weighed out|וָאֶשְׁקוֹלָה\rb* \rb to them|לָהֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the contribution|תְּרוּמַ֣ת\rb* \rb of silver|הַכֶּ֥סֶף\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb gold|הַזָּהָ֖ב\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the articles|הַכֵּלִ֑ים\rb* \rb that the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb*, \rb his counselors|וְיֹעֲצָ֣יו\rb*, \rb his leaders|וְשָׂרָ֔יו\rb*, \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb there|הַנִּמְצָאִֽים׃\rb* \rb had offered|הַהֵרִ֙ימוּ֙\rb* \rb for the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of our God|אֱלֹהֵ֗ינוּ\rb*.
\p \v 26 \rb I weighed out|וָאֶשְׁקֲלָ֨ה\rb* \rb into|עַל־\rb* \rb their hands|יָדָ֜ם\rb* \rb 650|שֵֽׁשׁ־\rb*\rb |מֵא֣וֹת\rb*\rb |וַחֲמִשִּׁ֔ים\rb* \rb talents|כִּכָּרִים֙\rb* \rb of silver|כֶּ֗סֶף\rb*,\f + \fr 8:26 \fqa 650 talents \ft is approximately 24.5 tons or 22.2 metric tons of silver.\f* \rb articles|וּכְלֵי־\rb* \rb of silver|כֶ֥סֶף\rb* \rb weighing 100|מֵאָ֖ה\rb* \rb talents|לְכִכָּרִ֑ים\rb*,\f + \fr 8:26 \fqa 100 talents \ft is approximately 3.77 tons or 3.42 metric tons of silver articles.\f* \rb 100|מֵאָ֥ה\rb* \rb talents|כִכָּֽר׃\rb* \rb of gold|זָהָ֖ב\rb*,\f + \fr 8:26 \fqa 100 talents \ft is approximately 3.77 tons or 3.42 metric tons of gold.\f* \v 27 \rb 20|עֶשְׂרִ֔ים\rb* \rb gold|זָהָב֙\rb* \rb bowls|וּכְפֹרֵ֤י\rb* \rb valued at 1,000|אָ֑לֶף\rb* \rb darics|לַאֲדַרְכֹנִ֖ים\rb*,\f + \fr 8:27 \ft Or \fqa worth 1,000 drachmas\ft ; that is, approximately 18.5 pounds or 8.4 kilograms of gold\f* \rb and two|שְׁנַ֔יִם\rb* \rb articles|וּכְלֵ֨י\rb* \rb of fine|טוֹבָה֙\rb* \rb polished|מֻצְהָ֤ב\rb* \rb bronze|נְחֹ֜שֶׁת\rb*, \rb as precious as|חֲמוּדֹ֖ת\rb* \rb gold|כַּזָּהָֽב׃\rb*.
\p \v 28 \rb Then I told|וָאֹמְרָ֣ה\rb* \rb them|אֲלֵהֶ֗ם\rb*, “\rb You|אַתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb are holy|קֹ֙דֶשׁ֙\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb and these articles are|וְהַכֵּלִ֖ים\rb* \rb holy|קֹ֑דֶשׁ\rb*. \rb The silver|וְהַכֶּ֤סֶף\rb* \rb and gold|וְהַזָּהָב֙\rb* \rb are a freewill offering|נְדָבָ֔ה\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of your fathers|אֲבֹתֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 29 \rb Guard them|שִׁקְד֣וּ\rb* \rb carefully|וְשִׁמְר֗וּ\rb* \rb until|עַֽד־\rb* \rb you weigh them out|תִּשְׁקְל֡וּ\rb* \rb in the chambers|הַלִּשְׁכ֖וֹת\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵי֩\rb* \rb the leading|שָׂרֵ֨י\rb* \rb priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֧ים\rb*, \rb Levites|וְהַלְוִיִּ֛ם\rb*, \rb and heads|וְשָׂרֵֽי־\rb* \rb of the Israelite|לְיִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb families|הָאָב֥וֹת\rb*.”
\p \v 30 \rb So the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֣ים\rb* \rb and Levites|וְהַלְוִיִּ֔ם\rb* \rb took charge of|וְקִבְּלוּ֙\rb* \rb the silver|הַכֶּ֥סֶף\rb* \rb and gold|וְהַזָּהָ֖ב\rb* \rb and sacred articles|וְהַכֵּלִ֑ים\rb* \rb that had been weighed out|מִשְׁקַ֛ל\rb* \rb to be taken|לְהָבִ֥יא\rb* \rb to the house|לְבֵ֥ית\rb* \rb of our God|אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ׃פ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|לִירוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb*.
\p \v 31 \rb On the twelfth|בִּשְׁנֵ֤ים\rb*\rb |עָשָׂר֙\rb* \rb day of the first|הָרִאשׁ֔וֹן\rb* \rb month|לַחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb* \rb we set out|וַֽנִּסְעָ֞ה\rb* \rb from the Ahava|אַֽהֲוָ֗א\rb* \rb Canal|מִנְּהַ֣ר\rb* \rb to go|לָלֶ֖כֶת\rb* \rb to Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb*, \rb and the hand|וְיַד־\rb* \rb of our God|אֱלֹהֵ֙ינוּ֙\rb* \rb was|הָיְתָ֣ה\rb* \rb upon us|עָלֵ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb to protect us|וַיַּ֨צִּילֵ֔נוּ\rb* \rb from the hands|מִכַּ֥ף\rb* \rb of the enemies|אוֹיֵ֛ב\rb* \rb and bandits|וְאוֹרֵ֖ב\rb* \rb along|עַל־\rb* \rb the way|הַדָּֽרֶךְ׃\rb*.
\s1 Arrival in Jerusalem
\p \v 32 \rb So we arrived|וַנָּב֖וֹא\rb* \rb at Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb and rested|וַנֵּ֥שֶׁב\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb for three|שְׁלֹשָֽׁה׃\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֥ים\rb*.
\p \v 33 \rb On the fourth|הָרְבִיעִ֡י\rb* \rb day|וּבַיּ֣וֹם\rb*, \rb in the house|בְּבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of our God|אֱלֹהֵ֗ינוּ\rb*, \rb we weighed out|נִשְׁקַ֣ל\rb* \rb the silver|הַכֶּסֶף֩\rb* \rb and gold|וְהַזָּהָ֨ב\rb* \rb and sacred articles|וְהַכֵּלִ֜ים\rb* \rb into|עַ֠ל\rb* \rb the hand|יַד־\rb* \rb of Meremoth|מְרֵמ֤וֹת\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Uriah|אֽוּרִיָּה֙\rb*, \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֔ן\rb*. \rb Eleazar|אֶלְעָזָ֣ר\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Phinehas|פִּֽינְחָ֑ס\rb* \rb was with him|וְעִמּ֖וֹ\rb*, \rb along with|וְעִמָּהֶ֞ם\rb* \rb the Levites|הַלְוִיִּֽם׃\rb* \rb Jozabad|יוֹזָבָ֧ד\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jeshua|יֵשׁ֛וּעַ\rb* \rb and Noadiah|וְנֽוֹעַדְיָ֥ה\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Binnui|בִּנּ֖וּי\rb*. \v 34 \rb Everything|לַכֹּ֑ל\rb* \rb was verified by number|בְּמִסְפָּ֥ר\rb* \rb and weight|בְּמִשְׁקָ֖ל\rb*, \rb and the total|כָּֽל־\rb* \rb weight|הַמִּשְׁקָ֖ל\rb* \rb was recorded|וַיִּכָּתֵ֥ב\rb* \rb at that|הַהִֽיא׃פ\rb* \rb time|בָּעֵ֥ת\rb*.
\p \v 35 \rb Then the exiles|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |הַגּוֹלָ֜ה\rb* \rb who had returned|הַ֠בָּאִים\rb* \rb from captivity|מֵֽהַשְּׁבִ֨י\rb* \rb sacrificed|הִקְרִ֥יבוּ\rb* \rb burnt offerings|עֹל֣וֹת׀\rb* \rb to the God|לֵאלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb*: \rb 12|שְׁנֵים־\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֤ר\rb* \rb bulls|פָּרִ֨ים\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb*, \rb 96|תִּשְׁעִ֣ים\rb*\rb |וְשִׁשָּׁ֗ה\rb* \rb rams|אֵילִ֣ים׀\rb*, \rb 77|שִׁבְעִ֣ים\rb*\rb |וְשִׁבְעָ֔ה\rb* \rb lambs|כְּבָשִׂים֙\rb*, \rb and a sin offering|חַטָּ֖את\rb* \rb of 12|שְׁנֵ֣ים\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֑ר\rb* \rb male goats|צְפִירֵ֥י\rb*. \rb All this was|הַכֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb a burnt offering|עוֹלָ֥ה\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָֽה׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 36 \rb They also delivered|וַֽיִּתְּנ֣וּ׀\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the king’s|הַמֶּ֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb edicts|דָּתֵ֣י\rb* \rb to the royal|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb satraps|לַאֲחַשְׁדַּרְפְּנֵי֙\rb*\f + \fr 8:36 \ft A \fqa satrap \ft was a Persian official.\f* \rb and governors|וּפַחֲו֖וֹת\rb* \rb of the region west|עֵ֣בֶר\rb* \rb of the Euphrates|הַנָּהָ֑ר\rb*,\f + \fr 8:36 \ft Hebrew \fqa governors beyond the River\f* \rb who proceeded to assist|וְנִשְּׂא֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the house|בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִֽים׃ס\rb*.
\c 9
\s1 Intermarriage with Neighboring Peoples
\p \v 1 \rb After these things|אֵ֗לֶּה\rb* \rb had been accomplished|וּכְכַלּ֣וֹת\rb*, \rb the leaders|הַשָּׂרִים֙\rb* \rb approached|נִגְּשׁ֨וּ\rb* \rb me|אֵלַ֤י\rb* \rb and said|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*, “\rb The people|הָעָ֤ם\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb*, \rb including the priests|וְהַכֹּהֲנִ֣ים\rb* \rb and Levites|וְהַלְוִיִּ֔ם\rb*, \rb have not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb kept themselves separate|נִבְדְּל֞וּ\rb* \rb from the surrounding|הָאֲרָצ֑וֹת\rb* \rb peoples|מֵעַמֵּ֖י\rb* \rb whose abominations|כְּ֠תוֹעֲבֹֽתֵיהֶם\rb* \rb are like those of the Canaanites|לַכְּנַעֲנִ֨י\rb*, \rb Hittites|הַחִתִּ֜י\rb*, \rb Perizzites|הַפְּרִזִּ֣י\rb*, \rb Jebusites|הַיְבוּסִ֗י\rb*, \rb Ammonites|הָֽעַמֹּנִי֙\rb*, \rb Moabites|הַמֹּ֣אָבִ֔י\rb*, \rb Egyptians|הַמִּצְרִ֖י\rb*, \rb and Amorites|וְהָאֱמֹרִֽי׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb Indeed|כִּֽי־\rb*, \rb the Israelites have taken|נָשְׂא֣וּ\rb* \rb some of their daughters as wives|מִבְּנֹֽתֵיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb for themselves|לָהֶם֙\rb* \rb and their sons|וְלִבְנֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb so that the holy|הַקֹּ֔דֶשׁ\rb* \rb seed|זֶ֣רַע\rb* \rb has been mixed|וְהִתְעָֽרְבוּ֙\rb* \rb with the people|בְּעַמֵּ֖י\rb* \rb of the land|הָאֲרָצ֑וֹת\rb*. \rb And the leaders|הַשָּׂרִ֣ים\rb* \rb and officials|וְהַסְּגָנִ֗ים\rb* \rb have taken the lead|וְיַ֧ד\rb*\rb |הָֽיְתָ֛ה\rb*\rb |רִאשׁוֹנָֽה׃ס\rb* \rb in this|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb unfaithfulness|בַּמַּ֥עַל\rb*!”
\p \v 3 \rb When I heard|וּכְשָׁמְעִי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb report|הַדָּבָ֣ר\rb*, \rb I tore|קָרַ֥עְתִּי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my tunic|בִּגְדִ֖י\rb* \rb and cloak|וּמְעִילִ֑י\rb*, \rb pulled out|וָאֶמְרְטָ֞ה\rb* \rb some hair|מִשְּׂעַ֤ר\rb* \rb from my head|רֹאשִׁי֙\rb* \rb and beard|וּזְקָנִ֔י\rb*, \rb and sat down|וָאֵשְׁבָ֖ה\rb* \rb in horror|מְשׁוֹמֵֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb Then everyone|כֹּ֤ל\rb* \rb who trembled|חָרֵד֙\rb* \rb at the words|בְּדִבְרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the God|אֱלֹהֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb gathered|יֵאָסְפ֗וּ\rb* \rb around me|וְאֵלַ֣י\rb* \rb because of|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb the unfaithfulness|מַ֣עַל\rb* \rb of the exiles|הַגּוֹלָ֑ה\rb*, \rb while I|וַאֲנִי֙\rb* \rb sat there|יֹשֵׁ֣ב\rb* \rb in horror|מְשׁוֹמֵ֔ם\rb* \rb until|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb the evening|הָעָֽרֶב׃\rb* \rb offering|לְמִנְחַ֥ת\rb*.
\s1 Ezra’s Prayer of Confession
\p \v 5 \rb At the evening|הָעֶ֗רֶב\rb* \rb offering|וּבְמִנְחַ֣ת\rb*, \rb I got up|קַ֚מְתִּי\rb* \rb from my humiliation|מִתַּֽעֲנִיתִ֔י\rb* \rb with my tunic|בִגְדִ֖י\rb* \rb and cloak|וּמְעִילִ֑י\rb* \rb torn|וּבְקָרְעִ֥י\rb*, \rb and I fell|וָֽאֶכְרְעָה֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb my knees|בִּרְכַּ֔י\rb*, \rb spread out|וָאֶפְרְשָׂ֥ה\rb* \rb my hands|כַפַּ֖י\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb my God|אֱלֹהָֽי׃\rb*, \v 6 \rb and said|וָאֹמְרָ֗ה\rb*:
\p “\rb O my God|אֱלֹהַי֙\rb*, \rb I am ashamed|בֹּ֣שְׁתִּי\rb* \rb and embarrassed|וְנִכְלַ֔מְתִּי\rb* \rb to lift up|לְהָרִ֧ים\rb* \rb my face|פָּנַ֖י\rb* \rb to You|אֵלֶ֑יךָ\rb*, \rb my God|אֱלֹהַ֛י\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb our iniquities|עֲוֺנֹתֵ֤ינוּ\rb* \rb are higher than|רָבוּ֙\rb*\rb |לְמַ֣עְלָה\rb* \rb our heads|רֹּ֔אשׁ\rb*, \rb and our guilt|וְאַשְׁמָתֵ֥נוּ\rb* \rb has reached|גָדְלָ֖ה\rb*\rb |עַ֥ד\rb* \rb the heavens|לַשָּׁמָֽיִם׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb From the days|מִימֵ֣י\rb* \rb of our fathers|אֲבֹתֵ֗ינוּ\rb* \rb to|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb*, \rb our guilt|בְּאַשְׁמָ֣ה\rb* \rb has been great|גְדֹלָ֔ה\rb*. \rb Because of our iniquities|וּבַעֲוֺנֹתֵ֡ינוּ\rb*, \rb we|אֲנַחְנוּ֩\rb* \rb and our kings|מְלָכֵ֨ינוּ\rb* \rb and priests|כֹהֲנֵ֜ינוּ\rb* \rb have been delivered|נִתַּ֡נּוּ\rb* \rb into the hands|בְּיַ֣ד׀\rb* \rb of the kings|מַלְכֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the earth|הָאֲרָצ֗וֹת\rb* \rb and subjected to the sword|בַּחֶ֜רֶב\rb* \rb and to captivity|בַּשְּׁבִ֧י\rb*, \rb to pillage|וּבַבִּזָּ֛ה\rb* \rb and humiliation|וּבְבֹ֥שֶׁת\rb*\rb |פָּנִ֖ים\rb*, \rb as we are this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb day|כְּהַיּ֥וֹם\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb But now|וְעַתָּ֡ה\rb*, \rb for a brief|כִּמְעַט־\rb* \rb moment|רֶגַע֩\rb*, \rb grace|תְחִנָּ֜ה\rb* \rb has come|הָיְתָ֨ה\rb* \rb from|מֵאֵ֣ת׀\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵ֗ינוּ\rb* \rb to preserve|לְהַשְׁאִ֥יר\rb* \rb for us|לָ֙נוּ֙\rb* \rb a remnant|פְּלֵיטָ֔ה\rb* \rb and to give|וְלָתֶת־\rb* \rb us|לָ֥נוּ\rb* \rb a stake|יָתֵ֖ד\rb*\f + \fr 9:8 \ft Or \fqa nail \ft or \fqa foothold\f* \rb in His holy|קָדְשׁ֑וֹ\rb* \rb place|בִּמְק֣וֹם\rb*. \rb Even in our bondage|בְּעַבְדֻתֵֽנוּ׃\rb*, \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb has given us|וּלְתִתֵּ֛נוּ\rb* \rb new life|מִֽחְיָ֥ה\rb*\rb |מְעַ֖ט\rb* \rb and light|לְהָאִ֤יר\rb* \rb to our eyes|עֵינֵ֙ינוּ֙\rb*. \v 9 \rb Though|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb we|אֲנַ֔חְנוּ\rb* \rb are slaves|עֲבָדִ֣ים\rb*, \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵ֑ינוּ\rb* \rb has not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb forsaken us|עֲזָבָ֖נוּ\rb* \rb in our bondage|וּבְעַבְדֻ֔תֵנוּ\rb*, \rb but He has extended|וַֽיַּט־\rb* \rb to us|עָלֵ֣ינוּ\rb* \rb grace|חֶ֡סֶד\rb* \rb in the sight|לִפְנֵי֩\rb* \rb of the kings|מַלְכֵ֨י\rb* \rb of Persia|פָרַ֜ס\rb*, \rb giving|לָֽתֶת־\rb* \rb us|לָ֣נוּ\rb* \rb new life|מִֽחְיָ֗ה\rb* \rb to rebuild|לְרוֹמֵ֞ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֤ית\rb* \rb of our God|אֱלֹהֵ֙ינוּ֙\rb* \rb and repair|וּלְהַעֲמִ֣יד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb its ruins|חָרְבֹתָ֔יו\rb*, \rb and giving|וְלָֽתֶת־\rb* \rb us|לָ֣נוּ\rb* \rb a wall of protection|גָדֵ֔ר\rb* \rb in Judah|בִּֽיהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb and Jerusalem|וּבִירוּשָׁלִָֽם׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb And now|וְעַתָּ֛ה\rb*, \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵ֖ינוּ\rb*, \rb what|מַה־\rb* \rb can we say|נֹּאמַ֥ר\rb* \rb after|אַֽחֲרֵי־\rb* \rb this|זֹ֑את\rb*? \rb For|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb we have forsaken|עָזַ֖בְנוּ\rb* \rb the commandments|מִצְוֺתֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \v 11 \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb You gave|צִוִּ֗יתָ\rb* \rb through|בְּיַ֨ד\rb* \rb Your servants|עֲבָדֶ֣יךָ\rb* \rb the prophets|הַנְּבִיאִים֮\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹר֒\rb*: ‘\rb The land|הָאָ֗רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֤ם\rb* \rb are entering|בָּאִים֙\rb* \rb to possess|לְרִשְׁתָּ֔הּ\rb* \rb is|הִ֔יא\rb* \rb a land|אֶ֤רֶץ\rb* \rb polluted|נִדָּה֙\rb* \rb by the impurity|בְּנִדַּ֖ת\rb* \rb of its peoples|עַמֵּ֣י\rb*\rb |הָאֲרָצ֑וֹת\rb* \rb and the abominations|בְּתוֹעֲבֹֽתֵיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb with which|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb they have filled it|מִלְא֛וּהָ\rb* \rb from end|מִפֶּ֥ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb end|פֶּ֖ה\rb*\rb |בְּטֻמְאָתָֽם׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb Now, therefore|וְ֠עַתָּה\rb*, \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb give|תִּתְּנ֣וּ\rb* \rb your daughters in marriage|בְּֽנוֹתֵיכֶ֞ם\rb* \rb to their sons|לִבְנֵיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb or take|תִּשְׂא֣וּ\rb* \rb their daughters|וּבְנֹֽתֵיהֶם֙\rb*\rb |אַל־\rb* \rb for your sons|לִבְנֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*. \rb Never|וְלֹֽא־\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb*\rb |עוֹלָ֑ם\rb* \rb seek|תִדְרְשׁ֧וּ\rb* \rb their peace|שְׁלֹמָ֛ם\rb* \rb or prosperity|וְטוֹבָתָ֖ם\rb*, \rb so that|לְמַ֣עַן\rb* \rb you may be strong|תֶּחֶזְק֗וּ\rb* \rb and may eat|וַאֲכַלְתֶּם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the good things|ט֣וּב\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb*, \rb leaving it as an inheritance|וְהוֹרַשְׁתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb to your sons|לִבְנֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb forever|עַד־\rb*\rb |עוֹלָֽם׃\rb*.’
\p \v 13 \rb After|וְאַֽחֲרֵי֙\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that has come|הַבָּ֣א\rb* \rb upon us|עָלֵ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb because of our evil|הָרָעִ֔ים\rb* \rb deeds|בְּמַעֲשֵׂ֙ינוּ֙\rb* \rb and our great|הַגְּדֹלָ֑ה\rb* \rb guilt|וּבְאַשְׁמָתֵ֖נוּ\rb* (\rb though|כִּ֣י׀\rb* \rb You|אַתָּ֣ה\rb*, \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵ֗ינוּ\rb*, \rb have punished us|חָשַׂ֤כְתָּֽ\rb* \rb less|לְמַ֙טָּה֙\rb* \rb than our iniquities deserve|מֵֽעֲוֺנֵ֔נוּ\rb* \rb and have given|וְנָתַ֥תָּה\rb* \rb us|לָּ֛נוּ\rb* \rb such a remnant|פְּלֵיטָ֖ה\rb* \rb as this|כָּזֹֽאת׃\rb*), \v 14 \rb shall we again|הֲנָשׁוּב֙\rb* \rb break|לְהָפֵ֣ר\rb* \rb Your commandments|מִצְוֺתֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb and intermarry|וּ֨לְהִתְחַתֵּ֔ן\rb* \rb with the peoples|בְּעַמֵּ֥י\rb* \rb who commit these|הָאֵ֑לֶּה\rb* \rb abominations|הַתֹּעֵב֖וֹת\rb*? \rb Would You not|הֲל֤וֹא\rb* \rb become so angry|תֶֽאֱנַף־\rb* \rb with us|בָּ֙נוּ֙\rb* \rb as to|עַד־\rb* \rb wipe us out|כַּלֵּ֔ה\rb*, \rb leaving no|לְאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb remnant|שְׁאֵרִ֖ית\rb* \rb or survivor|וּפְלֵיטָֽה׃פ\rb*?
\p \v 15 \rb O LORD|יְהוָ֞ה\rb*, \rb God|אֱלֹהֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb*, \rb You|אַ֔תָּה\rb* \rb are righteous|צַדִּ֣יק\rb*! \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb we remain|נִשְׁאַ֥רְנוּ\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb day|כְּהַיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb as a remnant|פְלֵיטָ֖ה\rb*. \rb Here we are|הִנְנ֤וּ\rb* \rb before You|לְפָנֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb in our guilt|בְּאַשְׁמָתֵ֔ינוּ\rb*, \rb though|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb because|עַל־\rb* \rb of it|זֹֽאת׃פ\rb* \rb no one|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb can stand|לַעֲמ֛וֹד\rb* \rb before You|לְפָנֶ֖יךָ\rb*.”
\c 10
\s1 Shecaniah’s Encouragement
\p \v 1 \rb While Ezra|עֶזְרָא֙\rb* \rb prayed|וּכְהִתְפַּלֵּ֤ל\rb* \rb and made this confession|וּכְ֨הִתְוַדֹּת֔וֹ\rb*, \rb weeping|בֹּכֶה֙\rb* \rb and falling facedown|וּמִתְנַפֵּ֔ל\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb*, \rb a very|מְאֹ֗ד\rb* \rb large|רַב־\rb* \rb assembly|קָהָ֣ל\rb* \rb of Israelites|מִיִּשְׂרָאֵ֜ל\rb* — \rb men|אֲנָשִׁ֤ים\rb*, \rb women|וְנָשִׁים֙\rb*, \rb and children|וִֽילָדִ֔ים\rb* — \rb gathered|נִקְבְּצוּ֩\rb* \rb around him|אֵלָ֨יו\rb*, \rb and the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb wept bitterly|בָכ֥וּ\rb*\rb |הַרְבֵּה־\rb*\rb |בֶֽכֶה׃ס\rb* \rb as well|כִּֽי־\rb*.
\p \v 2 \rb Then|וַיַּעַן֩\rb* \rb Shecaniah|שְׁכַנְיָ֨ה\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Jehiel|יְחִיאֵ֜ל\rb*, \rb an Elamite|מִבְּנֵ֤י\rb*\rb |עוֹלָם\rb*, \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to Ezra|לְעֶזְרָ֔א\rb*: “\rb We|אֲנַ֙חְנוּ֙\rb* \rb have been unfaithful|מָעַ֣לְנוּ\rb* \rb to our God|בֵאלֹהֵ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb by marrying|וַנֹּ֛שֶׁב\rb* \rb foreign|נָכְרִיּ֖וֹת\rb* \rb women|נָשִׁ֥ים\rb* \rb from the people|מֵעַמֵּ֣י\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*, \rb yet|וְעַתָּ֛ה\rb* \rb in spite of|עַל־\rb* \rb this|זֹֽאת׃\rb*, \rb there is|יֵשׁ־\rb* \rb hope|מִקְוֶ֥ה\rb* \rb for Israel|לְיִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*. \v 3 \rb So now|וְעַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb let us make|נִֽכְרָת־\rb* \rb a covenant|בְּרִ֣ית\rb* \rb before our God|לֵ֠אלֹהֵינוּ\rb* \rb to send away|לְהוֹצִ֨יא\rb* \rb all|כָל־\rb* \rb the foreign wives|נָשִׁ֜ים\rb* \rb and their children|וְהַנּוֹלָ֤ד\rb*,\rb |מֵהֶם֙\rb* \rb according to the counsel|בַּעֲצַ֣ת\rb* \rb of my lord|אֲדֹנָ֔י\rb* \rb and of those who tremble|וְהַחֲרֵדִ֖ים\rb* \rb at the command|בְּמִצְוַ֣ת\rb* \rb of our God|אֱלֹהֵ֑ינוּ\rb*. \rb Let it be done|יֵעָשֶֽׂה׃\rb* \rb according to the Law|וְכַתּוֹרָ֖ה\rb*. \v 4 \rb Get up|ק֛וּם\rb*, \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb this matter is|הַדָּבָ֖ר\rb* \rb your responsibility|עָלֶ֥יךָ\rb*, \rb and we|וַאֲנַ֣חְנוּ\rb* \rb will support you|עִמָּ֑ךְ\rb*. \rb Be strong|חֲזַ֖ק\rb* \rb and take action|וַעֲשֵֽׂה׃פ\rb*!”
\p \v 5 \rb So Ezra|עֶזְרָ֡א\rb* \rb got up|וַיָּ֣קָם\rb* \rb and made the leading|שָׂרֵי֩\rb* \rb priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֨ים\rb*, \rb Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֜ם\rb*, \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb take an oath|וַיַּשְׁבַּ֣ע\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to do what had been said|לַעֲשׂ֛וֹת\rb*\rb |כַּדָּבָ֥ר\rb*\rb |הַזֶּ֖ה\rb*. \rb And they took the oath|וַיִּשָּׁבֵֽעוּ׃\rb*.
\s1 The People’s Confession of Sin
\p \v 6 \rb Then Ezra|עֶזְרָ֗א\rb* \rb withdrew|וַיָּ֣קָם\rb* \rb from before|מִלִּפְנֵי֙\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of God|הָֽאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb and walked|וַיֵּ֕לֶךְ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the chamber|לִשְׁכַּ֖ת\rb* \rb of Jehohanan|יְהוֹחָנָ֣ן\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Eliashib|אֶלְיָשִׁ֑יב\rb*. \rb And while he stayed|וַיֵּ֣לֶךְ\rb*\f + \fr 10:6 \ft Or \fqa went\f* \rb there|שָׁ֗ם\rb*, \rb he ate|אָכַל֙\rb* \rb no|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb food|לֶ֤חֶם\rb* \rb and drank|שָׁתָ֔ה\rb* \rb no|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb water|וּמַ֣יִם\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb he was mourning|מִתְאַבֵּ֖ל\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the unfaithfulness|מַ֥עַל\rb* \rb of the exiles|הַגּוֹלָֽה׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb And a proclamation|ק֜וֹל\rb* \rb was issued|וַיַּעֲבִ֨ירוּ\rb* \rb throughout Judah|בִּיהוּדָ֣ה\rb* \rb and Jerusalem|וִירֽוּשָׁלִַ֗ם\rb* \rb that all|לְכֹל֙\rb* \rb the exiles|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |הַגּוֹלָ֔ה\rb* \rb should gather|לְהִקָּבֵ֖ץ\rb* \rb at Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb Whoever|וְכֹל֩\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb failed|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb to appear|יָב֜וֹא\rb* \rb within three|לִשְׁלֹ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb days|הַיָּמִ֗ים\rb* \rb would forfeit|יָחֳרַ֖ם\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb his property|רְכוּשׁ֑וֹ\rb*,\rb |וְה֥וּא\rb* \rb according to the counsel|כַּעֲצַ֤ת\rb* \rb of the leaders|הַשָּׂרִים֙\rb* \rb and elders|וְהַזְּקֵנִ֔ים\rb*, \rb and would himself be expelled|יִבָּדֵ֖ל\rb* \rb from the assembly|מִקְּהַ֥ל\rb* \rb of the exiles|הַגּוֹלָֽה׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb So within the three|לִשְׁלֹ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb days|הַיָּמִ֗ים\rb*, \rb all|כָל־\rb* \rb the men|אַנְשֵֽׁי־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָה֩\rb* \rb and Benjamin|וּבִנְיָמִ֨ן׀\rb* \rb assembled|וַיִּקָּבְצ֣וּ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֜ם\rb*,\rb |ה֛וּא\rb* \rb and on the twentieth day|בְּעֶשְׂרִ֣ים\rb*\rb |בַּחֹ֑דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of the ninth|הַתְּשִׁיעִ֖י\rb* \rb month|חֹ֥דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb all|כָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֗ם\rb* \rb sat|וַיֵּשְׁב֣וּ\rb* \rb in the square|בִּרְחוֹב֙\rb* \rb at the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb*, \rb trembling|מַרְעִידִ֥ים\rb* \rb regarding|עַל־\rb* \rb this matter|הַדָּבָ֖ר\rb* \rb and because of the heavy rain|וּמֵהַגְּשָׁמִֽים׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb Then Ezra|עֶזְרָ֤א\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵן֙\rb* \rb stood up|וַיָּ֨קָם\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to them|אֲלֵהֶ֔ם\rb*, “\rb You|אַתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb have been unfaithful|מְעַלְתֶּ֔ם\rb* \rb by marrying|וַתֹּשִׁ֖יבוּ\rb* \rb foreign|נָכְרִיּ֑וֹת\rb* \rb women|נָשִׁ֣ים\rb*, \rb adding|לְהוֹסִ֖יף\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the guilt|אַשְׁמַ֥ת\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb Now, therefore|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb*, \rb make|תְּנ֥וּ\rb* \rb a confession|תוֹדָ֛ה\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֥ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵֽי־\rb* \rb of your fathers|אֲבֹתֵיכֶ֖ם\rb*, \rb and do|וַעֲשׂ֣וּ\rb* \rb His will|רְצוֹנ֑וֹ\rb*. \rb Separate|וְהִבָּֽדְלוּ֙\rb* \rb yourselves|וּמִן־\rb* \rb from the people|מֵעַמֵּ֣י\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb and from your foreign|הַנָּכְרִיּֽוֹת׃\rb* \rb wives|הַנָּשִׁ֖ים\rb*.”
\p \v 12 \rb And the whole|כָֽל־\rb* \rb assembly|הַקָּהָ֛ל\rb*\rb |וַיֹּאמְר֖וּ\rb* \rb responded|וַיַּֽעְנ֧וּ\rb* \rb in a loud|גָּד֑וֹל\rb* \rb voice|ק֣וֹל\rb*: “\rb Truly|כֵּ֛ן\rb* \rb we must do|לַעֲשֽׂוֹת׃\rb* \rb as you say|כְּדִבְרֶיךָ\rb*\rb |עָלֵ֖ינוּ\rb*! \v 13 \rb But|אֲבָ֞ל\rb* \rb there are many|רָב֙\rb* \rb people here|הָעָ֥ם\rb*, \rb and it is the rainy|גְּשָׁמִ֔ים\rb* \rb season|וְהָעֵ֣ת\rb*. \rb We are not|וְאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb able|כֹּ֖חַ\rb* \rb to stay|לַעֲמ֣וֹד\rb* \rb out in the open|בַּח֑וּץ\rb*. \rb Nor is this|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb the work|וְהַמְּלָאכָ֗ה\rb* \rb of one|אֶחָד֙\rb* \rb or|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb two|לִשְׁנַ֔יִם\rb* \rb days|לְי֤וֹם\rb*, \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb we have transgressed|לִפְשֹׁ֖עַ\rb* \rb greatly|הִרְבִּ֥ינוּ\rb* \rb in this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb matter|בַּדָּבָ֥ר\rb*. \v 14 \rb Let our leaders|שָׂ֠רֵינוּ\rb* \rb represent|יַֽעֲמְדוּ־\rb*\rb |נָ֣א\rb* \rb the whole|לְֽכָל־\rb* \rb assembly|הַקָּהָ֞ל\rb*. \rb Then let everyone|וְכֹ֣ל׀\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb in our towns|בֶּעָרֵ֗ינוּ\rb* \rb who has married|הַהֹשִׁ֞יב\rb* \rb a foreign|נָכְרִיּוֹת֙\rb* \rb woman|נָשִׁ֤ים\rb* \rb come|יָבֹא֙\rb* \rb at an appointed|מְזֻמָּנִ֔ים\rb* \rb time|לְעִתִּ֣ים\rb*, \rb together with|וְעִמָּהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb the elders|זִקְנֵי־\rb* \rb and judges|וְשֹׁפְטֶ֑יהָ\rb*\rb |עַ֠ד\rb* \rb of each town|עִ֥יר\rb*\rb |וָעִ֖יר\rb*, \rb until the fierce anger|חֲר֤וֹן\rb*\rb |אַף־\rb* \rb of our God|אֱלֹהֵ֙ינוּ֙\rb*\rb |עַ֖ד\rb* \rb in this|הַזֶּֽה׃פ\rb* \rb matter|לַדָּבָ֥ר\rb* \rb is turned away|לְהָשִׁ֞יב\rb* \rb from us|מִמֶּ֔נּוּ\rb*.”
\p \v 15 (\rb Only|אַ֣ךְ\rb* \rb Jonathan|יוֹנָתָ֧ן\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Asahel|עֲשָׂהאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb and Jahzeiah|וְיַחְזְיָ֥ה\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Tikvah|תִּקְוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb supported|עֲזָרֻֽם׃\rb* \rb by Meshullam|וּמְשֻׁלָּ֛ם\rb* \rb and Shabbethai|וְשַׁבְּתַ֥י\rb* \rb the Levite|הַלֵּוִ֖י\rb*, \rb opposed|עָמְד֣וּ\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb this plan|זֹ֑את\rb*.)
\p \v 16 \rb So the exiles|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |הַגּוֹלָה֒\rb* \rb did|וַיַּֽעֲשׂוּ־\rb* \rb as proposed|כֵן֮\rb*. \rb Ezra|עֶזְרָ֨א\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֜ן\rb* \rb selected|וַיִּבָּדְלוּ֩\rb* \rb men|אֲנָשִׁ֨ים\rb* \rb who were family|הָאָב֛וֹת\rb* \rb heads|רָאשֵׁ֧י\rb*, \rb each of them|וְכֻלָּ֣ם\rb* \rb identified by name|בְּשֵׁמ֑וֹת\rb*,\rb |וַיֵּשְׁב֗וּ\rb* \rb to represent their families|אֲבֹתָ֖ם\rb*\rb |לְבֵ֥ית\rb*. \rb On the first|אֶחָד֙\rb* \rb day|בְּי֤וֹם\rb* \rb of the tenth|הָעֲשִׂירִ֔י\rb* \rb month|לַחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb* \rb they launched|לְדַרְי֖וֹשׁ\rb* \rb the investigation|הַדָּבָֽר׃\rb*, \v 17 \rb and by|עַ֛ד\rb* \rb the first|אֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb day|י֥וֹם\rb* \rb of the first|הָרִאשֽׁוֹן׃פ\rb* \rb month|לַחֹ֥דֶשׁ\rb* \rb they had dealt|וַיְכַלּ֣וּ\rb* \rb with all|בַכֹּ֔ל\rb* \rb the men|אֲנָשִׁ֕ים\rb* \rb who had married|הַהֹשִׁ֖יבוּ\rb* \rb foreign|נָכְרִיּ֑וֹת\rb* \rb women|נָשִׁ֣ים\rb*.
\s1 Those Guilty of Intermarriage
\p \v 18 \rb Among the descendants|מִבְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֔ים\rb* \rb who had married|הֹשִׁ֖יבוּ\rb* \rb foreign|נָכְרִיּ֑וֹת\rb* \rb women|נָשִׁ֣ים\rb* \rb were found|וַיִּמָּצֵא֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb these descendants|מִבְּנֵ֨י\rb* \rb of Jeshua|יֵשׁ֤וּעַ\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jozadak|יֽוֹצָדָק֙\rb*\f + \fr 10:18 \fqa Jozadak \ft is a variant of \fqa Jehozadak\ft ; see 1 Chronicles 6:14.\f* \rb and his brothers|וְאֶחָ֔יו\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \rb Maaseiah|מַֽעֲשֵׂיָה֙\rb*, \rb Eliezer|וֶֽאֱלִיעֶ֔זֶר\rb*, \rb Jarib|וְיָרִ֖יב\rb*, \rb and Gedaliah|וּגְדַלְיָֽה׃\rb*. \v 19 \rb They pledged|וַיִּתְּנ֥וּ\rb*\rb |יָדָ֖ם\rb* \rb to send their wives|נְשֵׁיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb away|לְהוֹצִ֣יא\rb*, \rb and for their guilt|וַאֲשֵׁמִ֥ים\rb* \rb they presented a ram|אֵֽיל־\rb* \rb from the flock|צֹ֖אן\rb* \rb as|עַל־\rb* \rb a guilt offering|אַשְׁמָתָֽם׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb From the descendants|וּמִבְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Immer|אִמֵּ֔ר\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \rb Hanani|חֲנָ֖נִי\rb* \rb and Zebadiah|וּזְבַדְיָֽה׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 21 \rb From the descendants|וּמִבְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Harim|חָרִ֑ם\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \rb Maaseiah|מַעֲשֵׂיָ֤ה\rb*, \rb Elijah|וְאֵֽלִיָּה֙\rb*, \rb Shemaiah|וּֽשְׁמַֽעְיָ֔ה\rb*, \rb Jehiel|וִיחִיאֵ֖ל\rb*, \rb and Uzziah|וְעֻזִיָּֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 22 \rb From the descendants|וּמִבְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Pashhur|פַּשְׁח֑וּר\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \rb Elioenai|אֶלְיוֹעֵינַ֤י\rb*, \rb Maaseiah|מַֽעֲשֵׂיָה֙\rb*, \rb Ishmael|יִשְׁמָעֵ֣אל\rb*, \rb Nethanel|נְתַנְאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb Jozabad|יוֹזָבָ֖ד\rb*, \rb and Elasah|וְאֶלְעָשָֽׂה׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 23 \rb Among|וּמִֽן־\rb* \rb the Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֑ם\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \rb Jozabad|יוֹזָבָ֣ד\rb*, \rb Shimei|וְשִׁמְעִ֗י\rb*, \rb Kelaiah|וְקֵֽלָיָה֙\rb* \rb (that is|ה֣וּא\rb*, \rb Kelita|קְלִיטָ֔א\rb*), \rb Pethahiah|פְּתַֽחְיָ֥ה\rb*, \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb*, \rb and Eliezer|וֶאֱלִיעֶֽזֶר׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 24 \rb From|וּמִן־\rb* \rb the singers|הַמְשֹׁרְרִ֖ים\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \rb Eliashib|אֶלְיָשִׁ֑יב\rb*.
\p \rb From|וּמִן־\rb* \rb the gatekeepers|הַשֹּׁ֣עֲרִ֔ים\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \rb Shallum|שַׁלֻּ֥ם\rb*, \rb Telem|וָטֶ֖לֶם\rb*, \rb and Uri|וְאוּרִֽי׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 25 \rb And among the other Israelites,|וּמִֽיִּשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb from the descendants|מִבְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Parosh|פַרְעֹ֡שׁ\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \rb Ramiah|רַ֠מְיָה\rb*, \rb Izziah|וְיִזִּיָּ֤ה\rb*, \rb Malchijah|וּמַלְכִּיָּה֙\rb*, \rb Mijamin|וּמִיָּמִ֣ן\rb*, \rb Eleazar|וְאֶלְעָזָ֔ר\rb*, \rb Malchijah|וּמַלְכִּיָּ֖ה\rb*,\f + \fr 10:25 \ft Hebrew; LXX \fqa Hashabiah\f* \rb and Benaiah|וּבְנָיָֽה׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 26 \rb From the descendants|וּמִבְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Elam|עֵילָ֑ם\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \rb Mattaniah|מַתַּנְיָ֤ה\rb*, \rb Zechariah|זְכַרְיָה֙\rb*, \rb Jehiel|וִיחִיאֵ֣ל\rb*, \rb Abdi|וְעַבְדִּ֔י\rb*, \rb Jeremoth|וִירֵמ֖וֹת\rb*, \rb and Elijah|וְאֵלִיָּֽה׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 27 \rb From the descendants|וּמִבְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Zattu|זַתּ֑וּא\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \rb Elioenai|אֶלְיוֹעֵנַ֤י\rb*, \rb Eliashib|אֶלְיָשִׁיב֙\rb*, \rb Mattaniah|מַתַּנְיָ֣ה\rb*, \rb Jeremoth|וִֽירֵמ֔וֹת\rb*, \rb Zabad|וְזָבָ֖ד\rb*, \rb and Aziza|וַעֲזִיזָֽא׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 28 \rb From the descendants|וּמִבְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Bebai|בֵּבָ֑י\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \rb Jehohanan|יְהוֹחָנָ֥ן\rb*, \rb Hananiah|חֲנַנְיָ֖ה\rb*, \rb Zabbai|זַבַּ֥י\rb*, \rb and Athlai|עַתְלָֽי׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 29 \rb From the descendants|וּמִבְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Bani|בָּנִ֑י\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \rb Meshullam|מְשֻׁלָּ֤ם\rb*, \rb Malluch|מַלּוּךְ֙\rb*, \rb Adaiah|וַעֲדָיָ֔ה\rb*, \rb Jashub|יָשׁ֖וּב\rb*, \rb Sheal|וּשְׁאָ֥ל\rb*, \rb and Jeremoth|יְרֵמוֹת׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 30 \rb From the descendants|וּמִבְּנֵ֛י\rb*\rb |פַּחַ֥ת\rb* \rb of Pahath-moab|מוֹאָ֖ב\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \rb Adna|עַדְנָ֣א\rb*, \rb Chelal|וּכְלָ֑ל\rb*, \rb Benaiah|בְּנָיָ֤ה\rb*, \rb Maaseiah|מַעֲשֵׂיָה֙\rb*, \rb Mattaniah|מַתַּנְיָ֣ה\rb*, \rb Bezalel|בְצַלְאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb Binnui|וּבִנּ֖וּי\rb*, \rb and Manasseh|וּמְנַשֶּֽׁה׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 31 \rb From the descendants|וּבְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Harim|חָרִ֑ם\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \rb Eliezer|אֱלִיעֶ֧זֶר\rb*, \rb Isshijah|יִשִּׁיָּ֛ה\rb*, \rb Malchijah|מַלְכִּיָּ֖ה\rb*, \rb Shemaiah|שְׁמַֽעְיָ֥ה\rb*, \rb Shimeon|שִׁמְעֽוֹן׃\rb*, \v 32 \rb Benjamin|בְּנְיָמִ֥ן\rb*, \rb Malluch|מַלּ֖וּךְ\rb*, \rb and Shemariah|שְׁמַרְיָֽה׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 33 \rb From the descendants|מִבְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Hashum|חָשֻׁ֑ם\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \rb Mattenai|מַתְּנַ֤י\rb*, \rb Mattattah|מַתַּתָּה֙\rb*, \rb Zabad|זָבָ֣ד\rb*, \rb Eliphelet|אֱלִיפֶ֔לֶט\rb*, \rb Jeremai|יְרֵמַ֥י\rb*, \rb Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁ֖ה\rb*, \rb and Shimei|שִׁמְעִֽי׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 34 \rb From the descendants|מִבְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Bani|בָנִ֔י\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \rb Maadai|מַעֲדַ֥י\rb*, \rb Amram|עַמְרָ֖ם\rb*, \rb Uel|וְאוּאֵֽל׃ס\rb*, \v 35 \rb Benaiah|בְּנָיָ֥ה\rb*, \rb Bedeiah|בֵדְיָ֖ה\rb*, \rb Cheluhi|כְּלָהַי׃\rb*, \v 36 \rb Vaniah|וַנְיָ֥ה\rb*, \rb Meremoth|מְרֵמ֖וֹת\rb*, \rb Eliashib|אֶלְיָשִֽׁיב׃\rb*, \v 37 \rb Mattaniah|מַתַּנְיָ֥ה\rb*, \rb Mattenai|מַתְּנַ֖י\rb*, \rb and Jaasu|וְיַעֲשׂוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 38 \rb From the descendants|וּבָנִ֥י\rb* \rb of Binnui|וּבִנּ֖וּי\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \rb Shimei|שִׁמְעִֽי׃\rb*,\f + \fr 10:38 \ft See LXX; Hebrew \fqa And Bani, and Binnui, (and) Shimei,\f* \v 39 \rb Shelemiah|וְשֶֽׁלֶמְיָ֥ה\rb*, \rb Nathan|וְנָתָ֖ן\rb*, \rb Adaiah|וַעֲדָיָֽה׃\rb*, \v 40 \rb Machnadebai|מַכְנַדְבַ֥י\rb*, \rb Shashai|שָׁשַׁ֖י\rb*, \rb Sharai|שָׁרָֽי׃\rb*, \v 41 \rb Azarel|עֲזַרְאֵ֥ל\rb*, \rb Shelemiah|וְשֶׁלֶמְיָ֖הוּ\rb*, \rb Shemariah|שְׁמַרְיָֽה׃\rb*, \v 42 \rb Shallum|שַׁלּ֥וּם\rb*, \rb Amariah|אֲמַרְיָ֖ה\rb*, \rb and Joseph|יוֹסֵֽף׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 43 \rb And from the descendants|מִבְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Nebo|נְב֑וֹ\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \rb Jeiel|יְעִיאֵ֤ל\rb*, \rb Mattithiah|מַתִּתְיָה֙\rb*, \rb Zabad|זָבָ֣ד\rb*, \rb Zebina|זְבִינָ֔א\rb*, \rb Jaddai|יַדּוֹ\rb*, \rb Joel|וְיוֹאֵ֖ל\rb*, \rb and Benaiah|בְּנָיָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 44 \rb All|כָּל־\rb* \rb these men|אֵ֕לֶּה\rb* \rb had married|נָשְׂא֖י\rb* \rb foreign|נָכְרִיּ֑וֹת\rb*\rb |וְיֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb women|נָשִׁ֣ים\rb*, \rb and some of them|מֵהֶ֣ם\rb* \rb had|וַיָּשִׂ֖ימוּ\rb* \rb children|בָּנִֽים׃פ\rb* \rb by these wives|נָשִׁ֔ים\rb*.\f + \fr 10:44 \ft Or \fqa and they sent them away with their children\f*
